      "description": "tag:www.troyuniversityjobs.com,2005:/postings/all_jobs Troy University: All Jobs 2026-09-03T09:03:54-05:00 https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48395 2026-09-03T09:03:54-05:00 2026-09-03T09:03:54-05:00 Assistant Director of Payroll Services <div>The Assistant Director of Payroll Services position serves as a strategic partner in leading all payroll operations for the university. This role provides hands-on oversight of payroll processing, compliance, and system administration while supporting the Director of Payroll in developing policies, implementing improvements, and ensuring exceptional service delivery. The Assistant Director manages day-to-day operations, supervises payroll staff, and serves as a subject matter expert on complex payroll matters affecting faculty, staff, graduate assistants, and student employees.</div> Payroll Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/45972 2025-11-12T09:32:11-06:00 2025-11-12T09:32:11-06:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor position in the College of Education at Dothan is a tenure-track position in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training. The position is responsible for teaching graduate courses in Rehabilitation and Clinical Mental Health Counseling; pursuit of scholarship and research; service on committees at all levels, and involvement in service to the community. This position also includes administrative responsibilities such as advising graduate students, supervising Practicum and Internship students, scheduling counseling courses, recruiting students for the program, proctoring and grading comprehensive examinations, attending faculty meetings, and attending required region meetings for faculty.</div> Department of C R I T - Dothan https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47526 2026-06-03T10:20:40-05:00 2026-06-03T10:20:41-05:00 Director, CMMS <div>The Center for Materials and Manufacturing Sciences within the School of Science and Technology at Troy University invites applications for the position of Director beginning as early as June 2024. The desired areas of expertise include Materials Chemistry, and/or Polymer Science/Engineering. The selected candidate will have considerable expertise in the synthesis, design, and recycling of plastics. The primary responsibilities of this position include scientific research, leadership in research and development for the Center, seeking external funds to sustain the Center and program development. The academic rank and tenure path will be discussed and negotiated during the final stages of the search process. Exceptional candidates from related science fields will also be considered for the position.</div> Chemistry and Physics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48210 2026-08-17T10:38:39-05:00 2026-08-17T10:38:40-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>Assist the Troy University IDEA Bank in event management, programmatic support, and daily administrative tasks. Primary duties include:</div><ul><li>Overseeing all bookable spaces at the IDEA Bank's downtown facility and coordinating event setup</li><li>Assisting members with room reservations, technology, and other member benefit fulfillment</li><li>Assisting walk-in guests with informational tours</li><li>Quality assurance of shared workspaces and technology</li><li>Scheduling and directing students for advising meetings</li><li>Membership Program execution, including data entry and assembly of new member packets/gifts</li><li>Marketing support, including social media assistance, graphic updates, flyer delivery, on-campus tabling, etc.</li><li>Assisting with Idea Vault Podcast Studio equipment setup and oversight</li><li>Assisting with Student-Made Store operations, including product labeling, store displays, etc.</li></ul><div><br>This position will work closely with the IDEA Bank Program and Marketing Coordinator and requires regular, reliable transportation to the IDEA Bank in downtown Troy.</div> IDEA Bank - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21584 2018-07-09T16:57:03-05:00 2023-05-24T10:09:22-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Psychology Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Department of Psychology https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46985 2026-04-08T09:57:34-05:00 2026-04-08T09:57:34-05:00 Archaeological Technician II <div>The Archaeological Technician II position is responsible for working with archaeological collections in the Troy University Archaeological Research Center laboratory. The curation tasks involve processing any newly acquired collections for curation, stabilizing existing collections, and maintaining an up-to-date inventory of all the collections. Primary duties include transferring artifacts into new bags and boxes that meet the curation standard. This position will also assist the anthropology faculty in ensuring that our collections meet federal guidelines related to the Native American Graves Repatriation and Protection Act (NAGPRA). Additionally, this position will have research opportunities with the Archaeology faculty.</div> Archaeological Research Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47925 2026-07-22T10:29:09-05:00 2026-07-22T10:29:10-05:00 Transcript Specialist II <div>The Transcript Specialist II position is responsible for but not limited to:<br><br></div><ul><li>Processing and issuing transcript requests both electronically and paper, including mail orders from other institutions, individual students and through Parchment.</li><li>Answering incoming calls to the department, assisting with transcript inquiries for current and former students, assists with ordering transcripts, and process for ordering unofficial transcripts, determining if transcripts have been received from other schools, answering all general questions regarding transcripts; assisting special investigators, employers, and other colleges with transcript inquiries, background checks, degree verifications, etc.</li><li>Managing departmental email, including processing and issuing transcripts, corresponding with other departments to assist in distribution of information in regards to transcripts.</li><li>Retrieve records from the vault and scan into document Imaging, scanning for Admissions as requested.</li><li>Issue course descriptions as requested</li><li>File records in vault after completion of document imaging process</li><li>Assist walk-in student’s with requests for transcripts, general questions, etc.</li><li>Other duties as required by supervisor</li></ul><div><br></div> Records Office - Global - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46800 2026-03-04T09:09:21-06:00 2026-03-04T09:09:21-06:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in the Admissions office is responsible for campus tours, telephone answering, and other clerical duties as assigned.</div> Admissions - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47769 2026-07-06T10:53:55-05:00 2026-07-06T10:53:55-05:00 Upward Bound Academic Teacher <div>The Upward Bound Academic Teacher position is responsible for preparing and conducting assigned classes in accordance with the overall design of the Upward Bound Program objectives.</div> Upward Bound - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48333 2026-08-27T11:01:52-05:00 2026-08-27T11:01:52-05:00 Workship - Scenic & Properties Shop Assistant <div>The Workship position for the Department of Theatre and Dance is responsible for serving as scene shop assistant, including organization and maintenance of materials, stock, and equipment, along with building or securing scenery for productions.</div> Theatre & Dance - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/36357 2022-11-17T16:09:44-06:00 2022-11-17T16:09:44-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Non-nursing Graduate Program <div><strong>Non-nurse Graduate Program Adjunct Instructor</strong><br><br>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Adjunct Instructors may teach no more than 8 semester hours per semester.</div> MSN Program https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47282 2026-05-14T12:24:29-05:00 2026-05-14T12:24:29-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position in Psychology is responsible for assisting the department chair and/or assigned faculty with any administrative duties related to research, assessment and accreditation information.</div> Department of Psychology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48014 2026-07-28T16:34:24-05:00 2026-07-28T16:34:25-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor of Political Science position in the College of Education and Behavioral Sciences is primarily responsible for teaching undergraduate courses in politics and law; pursuing a scholarship and research agenda; serving on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community; and advising students.</div> School of Social Sciences – Political Science - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21558 2018-07-09T16:55:45-05:00 2021-03-17T13:40:43-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Physics Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific Physics (lecture/lab) courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Physics https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47927 2026-07-22T10:30:30-05:00 2026-07-22T10:30:31-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Interpreter Training position in the College of Education &amp; Behavioral Sciences is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in clinical mental health counseling and other counseling specialties; pursuit of a scholarship and research agenda; service on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community; advising graduate students; and supervising Practicum and Internship students.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48397 2026-09-03T09:05:56-05:00 2026-09-03T09:05:57-05:00 Graduate Research Assistant - MSIR <div>The Center for Eastern and Central European, Russian, and Eurasian Studies (CECERES) at <em>Troy University</em> seeks a highly motivated <strong>Graduate Research Assistant</strong> to support the research activities of the Center Director and affiliated faculty. This position is designed for graduate students with strong analytical and writing skills who are interested in academic research, policy analysis, and international affairs.</div><div>The Graduate Research Assistant will contribute directly to faculty research projects, publications, grant proposals, and policy-oriented outputs related to Eastern and Central Europe, Russia, and Eurasia.</div><div><strong>About the Center:</strong><br> The Center for Eastern and Central European, Russian, and Eurasian Studies is an interdisciplinary research center focused on the politics, security, history, and societies of Eastern and Central Europe, Russia, and Eurasia. The Center supports faculty and student research, hosts scholarly and public events, and contributes to policy-relevant debates through research dissemination and external engagement.</div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>Conduct literature reviews and background research for faculty and Director-led projects.</div><div>Assist with data collection and organization, including qualitative and quantitative sources.</div><div>Support drafting and editing of academic manuscripts, policy briefs, reports, and grant applications.</div><div>Track developments related to regional politics, security, and international affairs.</div><div>Compile annotated bibliographies and research memorandum.</div><div>Assist with preparation of presentations, conference materials, and research summaries.</div><div>Support collaborative research projects involving multiple faculty members.</div> School of Social Sciences – Political Science - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46004 2025-11-17T09:05:28-06:00 2025-11-17T09:05:29-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - International Relations <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as needed basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught and are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issues on a semester/term basis&nbsp;</div> Political Science https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47528 2026-06-03T10:22:13-05:00 2026-06-03T10:22:14-05:00 Workship - Tutor <div>This position will allow for individuals to provide tutoring services to student-athletes as appointed through the Office of Student-Athlete Services. All tutoring appointments will take place in the Athletic Academic Center on the 3rd floor of the R. Douglas Hawkins Tower. As a tutor for the Office of Student-Athlete Services, it is imperative that tutors have a working understanding of NCAA rules and regulations as they apply to involvement with student-athletes. Failure to comply with NCAA regulations will automatically lead to the termination of your employment. If you have any questions regarding NCAA rules and how they apply to your tutorial activities, please contact the Office of Student-Athlete Services immediately.</div> Athletic Academic Enhancement - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48225 2026-08-18T12:31:22-05:00 2026-08-18T12:31:22-05:00 Police Officer <div>&nbsp;The Patrolman position in University Police is responsible for serving as a police officer by managing the safety and security of students, faculty, staff, visitors and property at the University; and working a specified shift with other officers to patrol all areas of the campus.</div> University Police - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21588 2018-07-09T16:57:12-05:00 2018-07-09T16:57:13-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Intern Supervisor The Intern Supervisor position in the Teacher Education Program is responsible for supervising and evaluating Education students in their internships in a P-12 setting; traveling to the schools and meeting with the students and cooperating teachers on a schedule recommended by the Office of Certification and Field Experiences; and reporting to the Department under the direction of the Director of Certification and Field Experiences. Department of Certification and Field Experience https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47023 2026-04-17T09:08:20-05:00 2026-04-17T09:08:21-05:00 Workship - Civic Life <div>This student worker position is responsible for leading the Civic Lab, supporting student engagement by connecting learning to real community needs through hands-on programming and partnerships, including a collaboration with the David Mathews Center for Civic Life. This role assists in planning and facilitating workshops and discussions for college students, while also working directly with youth in local schools to deliver activities related to civic responsibility and community involvement. Responsibilities include coordinating and leading volunteers, organizing events, supporting outreach efforts, and helping plan and implement initiatives such as a summer civics camp for elementary students. The position also involves collaborating with campus and community partners and assisting with basic program tracking and evaluation. This role also contributes to broader Office of Civic Engagement initiatives, helping connect students with meaningful opportunities to serve and engage in the community.</div> Civic Engagement - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21561 2018-07-09T16:55:56-05:00 2020-07-27T11:26:31-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Theatre and Dance The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching Theatre and Dance courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Theatre and Dance https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46900 2026-03-23T12:28:56-05:00 2026-03-23T12:28:57-05:00 Lecturer/Professor of Practice/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The <strong>Lighting Design &amp; Technolog</strong>y faculty position is a full-time position hired on a 10-month renewable contract. The open-rank posting allows for for authentic consideration of candidates’ unique strengths and potential to serve in the role of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Lecturer, or Professor of Practice. <br><br>The <strong>Lighting Design &amp; Technology</strong> faculty position in the Department of Theatre &amp; Dance is responsible for oversight of lighting, projections, and sound design and technology for productions; teaching courses in design, technology, and general theatre; producing quality theatrical lighting, projections, and sound that complement and support theatre and dance presentations; managing the department’s lighting and electrics shop; oversight of inventory, acquisition, organization, management, repair, and installation of technology and tools; supervising and training student crews in lighting and electrics; working within professional networks and organizations beyond the University; working with other Design and Technology faculty to develop curriculum and projects aimed specifically to students with goals and interests in the field of Design/Technology/Management; providing a focus on innovating and advancing ideas and practices in theatrical design and technology.</div> Theatre & Dance - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47771 2026-07-06T10:54:08-05:00 2026-07-06T10:54:09-05:00 Stagehand <div>The Stagehand position is responsible for assisting the Production Manager with the technical aspects of the theatre operations including but not limited to theatre maintenance, load-ins, load-outs, rehearsals, performances and other duties as assigned by the supervisor.</div> Davis Theatre - Montgomery https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48345 2026-08-27T13:21:59-05:00 2026-08-27T13:22:00-05:00 Academic Program Specialist <div>The Academic Program Specialist provides administrative support and manages a variety of academic and departmental processes for the School of Hospitality, Sport and Tourism Management, reporting to the Department Chair. This position is responsible for general office duties, scheduling, coordinating, and planning meetings, filing and recordkeeping, scholarship assistance, and assisting students and faculty as needed.</div> Hospitality, Sport, and Tourism Management - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/41199 2024-06-14T14:13:15-05:00 2024-06-14T14:13:16-05:00 Adjunct Instructor <div>The Adjunct Instructor position in Social Work and Human Services is responsible for teaching across a curriculum to include HBSE I and II, Social Policy, and Social Work Methods. In addition, this position may teach pre-practicum and Practicum. Options for on-line teaching are available. This position may also be asked to develop elective classes based on the areas of expertise.</div> Social Work - Phenix City https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47289 2026-05-14T15:23:50-05:00 2026-05-14T15:23:50-05:00 Regional Recruiter - Mississippi/Louisiana <div>Troy University Regional Recruiters are an essential element of the University’s Enrollment Management team. This role will be tasked with supporting Troy Campus traditional freshman and transfer student recruitment efforts in a defined geographic region by implementing recruiting strategies and activities that grow the number of students applying to TROY, being admitted to TROY, and ultimately choosing TROY for enrollment. Duties will include constant contact to prospective students and their families as well as establishing positive relationships with high schools, community colleges, and other sources of potential enrollments. Regional recruiters reside in their assigned geographic areas, but will travel to Troy Campus several times a year for training and professional development activities. (All official travel is covered for reimbursement.)<br><br>PLEASE NOTE: Applicants must reside in, or be willing to relocate to, the assigned geographic territory.</div> Admissions - Troy Online https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48057 2026-08-04T11:43:07-05:00 2026-08-04T11:43:08-05:00 Records Specialist II <div>The Records Specialist II position in the Academic Records Team is responsible for but not limited to:</div><ul><li>Assisting with registration for online and offshore students</li><li>Assisting with electronic routing of forms</li><li>Processing change of major forms</li><li>Processing change of minor forms</li><li>Processing Graduate readmissions</li><li>Processing Online Withdrawals, withdrawal Corrections, inactivating students</li><li>Performing other duties as assigned by supervisor</li></ul> Academic Records Team - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47079 2026-04-23T10:05:54-05:00 2026-04-23T10:05:55-05:00 Assistant Strength Coach <div>The Assistant Strenght Coach position is responsible for developing, implementing and maintaining a strength and conditioning program for all student-athletes; assisting in the day-to-day operations of the Weight Room; teaching sound lifting techniques to help ensure the safety of all student-athletes; being proactive with head coaches in developing programs that will asist in the prevention of athletic injuries; and providing assistance primarily for women's athletics.</div> Athletic Director - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47947 2026-07-23T11:24:45-05:00 2026-07-23T11:24:45-05:00 Lecturer <div>The Lecturer position in the Sorrell College of Business is a full-time, non-tenure track faculty appointment on a ten-month contract, beginning August 1, 2027.<br><br>The candidate will teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in marketing, entrepreneurship, or related areas. Candidates must possess appropriate academic qualifications in marketing, entrepreneurship, or a closely related field. Instruction will be delivered primarily on the Troy Campus, with regular online teaching responsibilities.<br><br>In addition to teaching, the candidate will be expected to collaborate with the Troy University IDEA Bank Student Entrepreneurship Center; engage in scholarly research and maintain faculty qualifications consistent with AACSB standards; advise students; and provide service to the department, college, university, profession, and community.</div> School of Creative Enterprise and Market Systems - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48403 2026-09-03T16:53:55-05:00 2026-09-03T16:53:55-05:00 Senior Support Analyst for Educational Technology <div>The Senior Support Analyst for Educational Technology position is responsible for troubleshooting Canvas LMS issues, completing helpdesk requests in a timely manner in a high-paced environment and assisting and training students, staff and faculty as needed; assisting and installing ancillary systems that interface into the Canvas LMS, including Plagiarism Detection System (TurnitIn), Respondus Lockdown Monitor/Browser/4.0 Exam Bank, NetTutor Online Tutoring and Camtasia; working daily in the Team Dynamix ticketing support system to address and resolve technical issues within Canvas; and developing training or informational presentations on the Canvas LMS to present to faculty at various training events.<br><br></div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21542 2018-07-09T16:55:04-05:00 2023-07-26T11:17:11-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Marketing The Adjunct Instructor position in Marketing is responsible for teaching Principles of Marketing and other undergraduate Marketing courses.  Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Marketing https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46164 2025-12-09T12:53:36-06:00 2025-12-09T12:53:37-06:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The College of Education at Troy University is seeking candidates for a full-time Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor (dependent on experience) position in the graduate-level Adult Education Program. This position will be housed in the Leadership Development &amp; Professional Studies Department. Responsibilities include teaching and advising graduate students; developing partnerships and collaborating with community colleges, military, &amp; business industry; maintaining open communication with partners, faculty, staff, &amp; administration; and other duties and responsibilities as identified by the departmental leadership. The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor position in Leadership Development and Professional Studies is responsible for teaching, advising, conducting research, providing university and community service, and participating in departmental, college, and university committees and activities.</div> Department of Leadership, Development and Professional Studies - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47578 2026-06-09T15:03:09-05:00 2026-06-09T15:03:09-05:00 Departmental Secretary I <div>The Departmental Secretary I position in Biology is responsible for providing secretarial support to the department through a variety of routine office clerical duties such as preparation of documents, scheduling appointments, directing calls, recording meetings, maintaining calendar of events, opening and distributing incoming mail, keeping files and records for the department, assisting students, and other duties as assigned.</div> Biology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48253 2026-08-19T11:24:26-05:00 2026-08-19T11:24:27-05:00 Financial Aid Counselor <div>The Financial Aid and Veterans Affairs Counselor position is responsible for providing counseling services related to student financial aid and veterans affairs to students and their families; processing financial aid and VA paperwork; disseminating information regarding financial aid and VA programs to prospective and enrolled students; meeting with students and families one-on-one and in groups to talk about financial aid and VA; engaging in student financial aid and VA educational sessions on and off campus; heavy contact with students and families via email, phone, and in-person; communicating as needed with all administrative offices of the University; and other duties as assigned by the supervisor.</div> Financial Aid - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21592 2018-07-09T16:57:25-05:00 2018-07-09T16:57:26-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Field Experiences Supervisor The Adjunct Instructor - Field Experiences Supervisor position in the Interpreter Training Program is responsible for reporting to the Interpreter Training Program Director; acting as the main point of contact between the Internship Mentor and the Program; and oversight and management of the Practicum and/or Internship class.  There is one supervisor for each Internship (Community/Education). \r\n\r\nAdjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis.  Adjunct instructors hold the responsibility for the management of assigned courses taught.  Adjunct instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.  Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Department of C R I T - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21563 2018-07-09T16:56:01-05:00 2019-12-11T13:45:47-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Law Adjunct faculty are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Law https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46911 2026-03-24T13:47:32-05:00 2026-03-24T13:47:33-05:00 Assistant Professor <div>The full-time, tenure-track faculty position of Assistant Professor of Accounting for the Sorrell College of Business/ Carr School of Accountancy is responsible for, but are not limited to: teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Accounting; leadership in program development at the undergraduate and graduate level in Accounting; engagement in scholarly activities; mentoring faculty; advising students; commitment to service to the University and community; and other duties as identified by the Director of the School of Accountancy and Dean of the College of Business.</div> School of Accountancy - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47773 2026-07-06T10:56:05-05:00 2026-07-06T10:56:05-05:00 Peer Tutor <div>The Peer Tutor position is responsible for providing tutorial assistance to Upward Bound students based on academic needs.</div> Upward Bound - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48352 2026-08-27T16:09:51-05:00 2026-08-27T16:09:51-05:00 Public Radio Membership Officer <div>The Public Radio Membership Officer is responsible for supporting Troy Public Radio's fundraising efforts by working with members of the station's sustaining member program; assisting in planning the station's regular fund drives and mail campaigns; and directly responsible for overseeing the fund drive call center.</div> Broadcast and Digital Network - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/43508 2025-02-27T08:19:37-06:00 2025-02-27T08:19:37-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - TROY 1101 <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> First Year Studies - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47306 2026-05-15T09:36:09-05:00 2026-05-15T09:36:10-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position in the College of Education is responsible for assisting the Dean with daily office duties, including answering the phone; entering and collecting data; use of Word, Excel, and Power Point; completing spread sheets; assisting College of Education students and faculty; and completion of a professional project that may include a research project, a presentation at a professional conference, or a specialized professional project designed by the Dean.</div> College of Education and Behavioral Sciences - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48059 2026-08-04T11:45:09-05:00 2026-08-04T11:45:09-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position in the Associate Provost's and Dean of the Graduate School's Office is responsible for performing general clerical and administrative support duties for the Graduate School.</div> Graduate School - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47177 2026-05-05T16:39:07-05:00 2026-05-05T16:39:08-05:00 Assistant Basketball Coach <div>The Assistant Basketball Coach position in Athletics is responsible for assisting in the planning, implementation and administration of the mens basketball program; and ensuring the program adheres to all applicable NCAA, conference and institutional rules and regulations.</div> Athletics - Basketball - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47955 2026-07-23T13:57:44-05:00 2026-07-23T13:57:45-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position for the College of Science and Engineering is responsible for performing lab monitoring, assisting the IT staff with the daily operations of computer labs, including troubleshooting, installation of hardware and software, etc., and other duties as assigned by the Dean's Office.</div> College of Science and Engineering - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21544 2018-07-09T16:55:08-05:00 2018-07-09T16:55:09-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Geography Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as needed basis.  Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught and are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issues on a semester/term basis. Geography https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46356 2026-01-12T08:36:54-06:00 2026-01-12T08:36:54-06:00 Adjunct Instructor <div>&nbsp;The adjunct faculty position in the Sorrell College of business is responsible for teaching courses in QM. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a term basis. Adjunct faculty members are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Specific expectations of adjunct faculty will be explained through coordination with the respective chair in the Sorrell College of Business.&nbsp;</div> Decision Systems and Sciences - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47597 2026-06-10T16:17:10-05:00 2026-06-10T16:17:11-05:00 Vision Rehabilitation Assistant <div>PLEASE NOTE: Position is located in <strong>Talladega, AL <br><br></strong>The Vision Rehabilitation Assistant position is responsible for:</div><ul><li>Interact with public so that ADRS is represented in a positive manner via phone or in person.</li><li>Transport and accompany State Coordinator of Blind Services on a statewide basis including extensive overnight and occasional weekend travel.</li><li>Complete travel forms, time sheets, and leave requests in a timely manner.</li><li>Maintain Outlook Calendar.</li><li>Inventory and monitor program supplies.</li><li>Prepare and distribute handouts/reports.</li><li>Read written correspondence for Coordinator of Blind Services.</li><li>Order and organize supplies for special programs.</li><li>Utilize computer and assistive technology to transcribe materials for State Coordinator of Blind Services and other staff in an accessible format (Braille, large print, and electronic).</li><li>Perform other duties as assigned by State Coordinator of Blind Services.</li></ul> Human Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48256 2026-08-19T11:59:39-05:00 2026-08-19T11:59:40-05:00 Assistant Strength Coach <div>The Assistant Strength Coach position in the Athletic Director department is responsible for implementing and maintaining a strength and conditioning program for all student athletes; assisting in the daily operations of the Weight Room; teaching sound techniques to help ensure the safety of all student athletes; being proactive with head coaches in developing programs that will assist in the prevention of athletic injuries; and providing assistance for all sport teams.</div> Athletic Director - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21632 2018-07-09T16:59:03-05:00 2018-07-09T16:59:04-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Instructional Leadership Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.\r\n\r\nThe Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching master-level and education specialist-level courses in an online format and/or in-class. Leadership Development and Professional Studies https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48065 2026-08-04T14:22:39-05:00 2026-08-04T14:22:40-05:00 Systems and Security Administrator <div>The Systems and Security Administrator position in Information Technology is responsible for providing technical and service-related support to the University through the application of computer science knowledge. This position will be heavily involved in cybersecurity process within the University.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21565 2018-07-09T16:56:08-05:00 2022-07-14T10:44:28-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Kinesiology and Health Promotion Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. School of Allied Health https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46941 2026-03-31T11:04:56-05:00 2026-03-31T11:04:57-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Health Services Administration <div>The Adjunct Instructor position in Health Services Administration is responsible for teaching graduate health services administration/management courses.<br><br>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> School of Management https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47776 2026-07-06T11:04:14-05:00 2026-07-06T11:04:14-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position serves to implement programming in the Office of Civic Engagement. Student workers are responsible for communicating effectively with internal and external stakeholders; taking initiative to plan, organize and implement academic and co-curricular programming; multitasking and working in a fast-paced environment; assisting with administrative support; working with local youth and seniors; flexibility to change plans regularly to meet adapting needs; contributing to a positive environment for colleagues and volunteers; other duties as assigned.</div> Civic Engagement - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48365 2026-08-31T09:12:24-05:00 2026-08-31T09:12:25-05:00 Annual Giving & Special Projects Coordinator <div>The Annual Giving &amp; Special Projects Coordinator position supports the university's annual giving program through donor stewardship, gift pipeline coordination, and appeals strategy, while also planning and executing special events that strengthen fundraising and donor engagement. This position plays a key role in advancing the office's vision to enhance alumni engagement with the university, deans, and faculty, and serves as a consistent point of connection between alumni, academic leadership, and the broader campus community.<br><br></div><div><strong>Essential Duties and Responsibilities</strong></div><div>● Coordinate the annual giving gift pipeline, tracking prospects and donors through each stage of the solicitation and stewardship cycle</div><div>● Support the development and execution of annual giving appeals strategy, including direct mail, email, crowdfunding, and digital campaigns</div><div>● Draft and coordinate donor communications, acknowledgment letters, and stewardship materials</div><div>● Monitor annual giving metrics and prepare regular progress reports for office leadership</div><div>● Partner with the advancement services team to ensure accurate gift processing, data integrity, and donor records</div><div>● Plan, coordinate, and execute special events related to fundraising and donor engagement, including donor recognition events, giving day campaigns, and alumni engagement events</div><div>● Manage event logistics, including venue coordination, vendor relationships, budgets, invitations, and day-of execution</div><div>● Collaborate with academic deans, faculty, and campus partners to plan events that connect alumni with the university's academic mission</div><div>● Evaluate event outcomes and donor engagement impact, recommending improvements for future initiatives</div><div>● Develop and maintain strong working relationships with deans, faculty, and academic departments to identify engagement and giving opportunities</div><div>● Serve as a liaison between the annual giving program and academic units to align fundraising priorities with institutional goals</div><div>● Support broader advancement office initiatives and special projects as assigned</div> Annual Giving https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/44550 2025-06-24T10:27:19-05:00 2025-08-04T13:41:07-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Anthropology <div>The Department of Anthropology, Sociology, and Criminology at Troy University invites applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty in Anthropology with preference given to those with expertise in cultural anthropology and/or linguistics to begin in the fall of 2025. Successful candidates will be able to offer courses that expand and support our existing curriculum at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The position will include teaching up to 8 credit hours per semester.</div> Anthropology https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47455 2026-05-29T11:49:24-05:00 2026-05-29T11:49:25-05:00 Helpdesk Operator III <div>The Helpdesk Operator III position in Information Technology is responsible for providing helpdesk support and escalating helpdesk calls as needed through the helpdesk software; understanding Troy’s processes and ensuring faculty, staff, and students receive exceptional support from IT; assisting the IT Facility Manager and Senior Support Specialist; managing all University-owned cellular devices, ensuring they work, making sure plans are accurate and up-to-date in the system; and assisting in new orders, upgrades, and disposal of devices and assisting in set-up, back-ups, and wiping of devices.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/26762 2019-10-23T09:53:16-05:00 2022-08-04T10:25:30-05:00 Adjunct Instructor-Geospatial Informatics The Adjunct Instructor will be responsible for teaching various undergraduate classes in the Geospatial Informatics Department\r\n\r\nAdjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Geospatial Informatics - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47179 2026-05-06T08:43:58-05:00 2026-05-06T08:43:58-05:00 Residential Advisor/Tutor <div>The Residential Advisor/Tutor position is responsible for providing tutorial assistance to Upward Bound students based on academic needs; supervising and monitoring Upward Bound students while on campus; enforcing resident hall and program rules; planning and implementing evening activities; and attending staff meetings.</div> Upward Bound - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47961 2026-07-23T15:55:13-05:00 2026-07-23T15:55:14-05:00 Director of International Enrollment Management <div>The Director of International Enrollment Management position is responsible for recruitment of international students to Troy University; developing promotional materials for international programs and activities; coordinating recruiting for all Troy University locations including Troy University teaching sites abroad; working to diversify the international student population; analyze enrollment trends and set strategic recruiting plans; train and mentor staff to successfully recruit and admit international students; prepare weekly and monthly application and admissions reports; analyzing current agent partnerships; reporting on success; recommending continuation (or not) of agreements while also vetting potential new agent partners; maintaining correspondence with potential international students and agents; assisting agencies in placing students at Troy University; and supervising employees and student workers.</div> International Programs - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21549 2018-07-09T16:55:22-05:00 2025-09-03T14:41:22-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Economics The Adjunct Instructor position in Economics is responsible for teaching beginning level Economics courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Economics https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46665 2026-02-12T11:38:56-06:00 2026-02-12T11:38:56-06:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor position in Psychology is responsible for: teaching courses in the area of Applied Behavior Analysis and/or other graduate and undergraduate psychology courses; advising and mentoring students; developing a research agenda; providing service to the community, profession, department, college, and university; and other duties as assigned by the department chair. The position is located at the Troy Campus in Troy, AL and is under the supervision of the Department of Psychology Chair. Troy University offers an undergraduate minor in Applied Behavior Analysis.</div> Department of Psychology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47636 2026-06-11T11:35:40-05:00 2026-06-11T11:35:40-05:00 Senior Security Analyst <div>The Senior Security Analyst position is responsible for technical and thought-leadership duties for multiple information security disciplines such as incident response, vulnerability management, intrusion detection and prevention, threat hunting, security operations, security policy, and awareness/education; oversight of information security incident response activities, risk assessment and risk management activities, and vulnerability assessment and vulnerability management activities spanning University and business units; managing detailed network, operating system, database, and application vulnerability assessments and security configuration audits; managing information security initiatives; oversight of operational tasks supporting information security functions such as intrusion detection and prevention, security event log analysis, management reporting, malware prevention and remediation, encryption, network segmentation, remote access, cloud security, and authentication; supporting, maintaining, monitoring, troubleshooting and enhancing security infrastructure tools, methodologies, software, and hardware; drafting and reviewing information security policies, processes, and procedures; reviewing information security awareness and education materials and other documentation; determining and documenting information security requirements and controls necessary for the protection of information resources; providing guidance and assistance regarding information security matters such as the interpretation of information security policies and requirements or their applicability to particular situations; independently maintaining automated tools and methodologies in support of Information Security functions; analyzing data from Information Security functions and providing reports and recommended response actions to Information Security management; representing Information Security to other organizations on information security related matters, as assigned; publishing regular status reports and submission to management; and performing other related tasks as assigned.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48272 2026-08-21T09:47:58-05:00 2026-08-21T09:47:58-05:00 Administrative Secretary <div>Provide administrative support to dean's office and departments of CCFA</div> College of Arts and Humanities - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47508 2026-06-01T17:02:37-05:00 2026-06-01T17:02:38-05:00 Undergraduate Research Assistant <div>The Undergraduate Research Assistantin Biological and Environmental Sciences is responsible for conducting biotic surveys in south Alabama associated with the Blackwater Wetland Gradient study. This work includes but is not limited to: traveling to field<br>locations, collecting data, completing data sheets, and participating in data entry and analysis.</div> Biology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48119 2026-08-06T12:10:11-05:00 2026-08-06T12:10:11-05:00 Academic Advisor/Life Skills <div>The Academic Advisor/Life Skills Coordinator position in the Athletics Department is responsible for overseeing the coordination of a minimum of four annual Life Skills events covering NCAA mandated mental health and student-athlete development areas; coordinating and monitoring study hall; and advising student-athletes, focusing primarily on assigned sports, including academic course advising as well as advising and counseling on daily issues such as social and athletic stressors vital to overall student well-being.</div> Athletic Reinforcement Programs - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21567 2018-07-09T16:56:15-05:00 2023-08-04T12:02:33-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Human Services The Adjunct Instructor position in Human Services is responsible for teaching across a curriculum to include HBSE I and II, Survey, Professional Communication, and electives as needed; may also supervise pre-practicum and practicum courses; and may also be asked to develop elective classes based on the areas of expertise.\r\nAdjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Human Services https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46974 2026-04-08T09:46:29-05:00 2026-04-08T09:46:30-05:00 Lecturer - Data Analytics <div>The Lecturer position in Data Analytics is responsible for a commitment to quality teaching, advising, and scholarly activity consistent with AACSB accreditation. The Lecturer will teach courses for the Carr School of Accountancy at both the graduate and undergraduate levels in topics related to data analytics. Courses may be taught online, hybrid, internationally, or in a traditional classroom setting.<br><br>The appointment is available for the 2025-2026 academic year beginning August 1, 2025. Applications will be accepted until a successful candidate is identified.</div> Decision Systems and Sciences - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47778 2026-07-06T11:06:26-05:00 2026-07-06T11:06:27-05:00 ALFA Eminent Scholar Graduate Fellow <div>The ALFA Eminent Scholar Graduate Fellow is responsible for:<br>- research activities such as collection, identification, photography, and database management for protozoans and microinvertebrates collected from the Gulf of Mexico and freshwater habitats;<br>- protozoan isolation, meiofauna isolation (centrifugation), counting, histochemistry and microscopic preparation of samples as assigned;<br>- laboratory maintenance and cleaning, inventory, assisting with scientific articles, writing drafts, running statistical tests., and creating maps using GIS. The applicant will be trained in these areas of responsibility.<br><br>This position has a starting date of May 25th or August 1st, 2026 depending on the applicant's availability.</div> Biology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48379 2026-09-01T17:21:48-05:00 2026-09-01T17:21:49-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant- Creative Media <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position in Marketing &amp; Communication is responsible for assisting in the visual story telling for TROY through compelling photography and video content.</div> Marketing & Communications - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/44552 2025-06-24T10:29:04-05:00 2025-06-24T10:29:04-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - History <div>The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching courses including the American, Western Civilization, and/or World History surveys. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> History https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48294 2026-08-24T12:19:25-05:00 2026-08-24T12:19:25-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in the Academic Evaluation Center is responsible for assisting the department with clerical duties, running errands, and will aid with Graduation Center or Records tasks, when needed.</div> Academic Evaluation Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/30035 2021-02-22T08:38:43-06:00 2021-07-12T09:45:54-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Integrated Arts The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching Integrated Arts courses, including courses in the 3D Printing for Art and Industry minor and other cross-disciplinary courses. \r\n\r\nAdjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Theatre and Dance https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47183 2026-05-06T08:49:03-05:00 2026-05-06T08:49:03-05:00 Band Event Staff - Basketball Pep Band <div>The Band Event Staff position is responsible for playing with the Sound of the South Pep Band at any function as needed.</div> Band - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47979 2026-07-27T08:37:11-05:00 2026-07-27T08:37:12-05:00 Peer Tutor <div>The duties of the Peer Tutor in Student Support Services include:</div><ul><li>Providing academic support in a designated discipline with the goal of reducing student attrition and increasing completion of required college courses</li><li>Providing individual and group coaching in writing, math, and/or study skills</li><li>Maintaining academic progress files on all tutored participants</li><li>Other duties as assigned by the Project Coordinator</li></ul> Student Support Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21551 2018-07-09T16:55:28-05:00 2024-02-19T08:21:45-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Information Systems The Adjunct Instructor position in Information Systems is responsible for teaching IS courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Information Systems https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46793 2026-03-04T09:02:14-06:00 2026-03-04T09:02:14-06:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in Residence Halls is responsible for serving as a Resident Assistant; serving students that have needs in the residence halls; serving as a point of contact as visitors come to the residence halls to visit residents; assisting with maintaining a secure environment in the residence halls; and assisting the Community Director in the performance of his/her duties in the administration of the residence halls.</div> Residence Halls - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47648 2026-06-16T14:08:09-05:00 2026-06-16T14:08:10-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in Geospatial Informatics is responsible for maintenance of Geomatics lab equipment, computer lab and any other task necessary to the operation of the department and its programs, to include some clerical work and recruitment activities</div> Geospatial Informatics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/44554 2025-06-24T10:30:50-05:00 2025-06-24T10:30:51-05:00 Adjunct Faculty - Game Design <div>Troy University seeks adjunct faculty members to teach online classes in our Game Design and Development minor. These classes may include History of Game Design, History Through Games, Game Development, Special Topics in Game Design and Development, and the Game Design and Development capstone class. The preferred applicant will have experience in tabletop game design and development, including role-playing, board, and/or card games.&nbsp;<br>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a term or semester basis. Adjunct instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. They are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> History - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47520 2026-06-03T09:52:50-05:00 2026-06-03T09:52:51-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor position of Counseling &amp; Psychology in the College of Education at Troy University's main campus is a tenure-track, ten-month faculty appointment. The rank is open and will be dependent upon experience and training. The primary responsibilities include teaching specialized graduate courses in school counseling and other counseling specialties; pursuing a scholarship and research agenda; serving on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community; advising graduate students; and supervising Practicum and Internship students.</div> Department of C R I T - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48163 2026-08-10T15:35:49-05:00 2026-08-10T15:35:50-05:00 Assistant Golf Coach <div>The Assistant Golf Coach position is responsible for assisting in management of all aspects of an NCAA Division I athletic program and interacting effectively and appropriately with student-athletes, parents, alumni, faculty, administrators, peers, and community members; assist in the evaluation of prospects; maintaining and ensuring student-athlete academic integrity; demonstrating a commitment to the mission and values of Troy University; complying with NCAA, conference, and university rules and regulations; assist in the coordination of practice and match/tournament day preparation and scheduling; recruiting and graduating student-athletes for the golf program; and other duties as assigned.</div> Athletics - Golf - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21575 2018-07-09T16:56:40-05:00 2025-07-02T13:43:18-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Journalism and Communication The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching courses in Journalism and Communication. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Journalism and Communication https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46979 2026-04-08T09:52:34-05:00 2026-04-08T09:52:34-05:00 Customer Service Representative <div>The Customer Service Representative position is responsible for assisting customers (primarily TROY students and parents) by answering incoming phone calls regarding financial aid, admissions, student account services, enrollment management, and other related departmental areas in an effort to answer inquiries, resolve issues, and fulfill requests. Staff will also assist with clerical duties during the call center’s off-peak periods as needed.<br>Other job duties include:<br>• Answers inquiries by clarifying desired information; researching, locating, and providing information.<br>• Resolves problems by clarifying issues; researching and exploring answers and alternative solutions; implementing solutions; escalating unresolved problems.<br>• Logs communications in database.<br>• Keeps equipment operational by following established procedures; reporting malfunctions.<br>• Provides general office support that assists in the functioning of the office including basic computer data entry, filing paperwork, sending and receiving faxes, and relaying messages.</div> Troy Online - Call Center https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47872 2026-07-16T15:21:23-05:00 2026-07-16T15:21:24-05:00 Donor Relations Specialist <div>The Donor Relations Specialist position will serve as a member of the Office of Development and will play a key role in donor relations. The Donor Relations Specialist position will help implement a program with a goal of nurturing positive relationships with leadership donors. The program is composed primarily of donor relations, which includes cultivating and stewarding long-term relationships with leadership donors, as well as strategic and creative thinking around how to advance stewardship to a more sophisticated and personalized level. This individual will join a team that is committed to increasing philanthropic support of Troy University.<br><strong>Responsibilities/Duties</strong><br>-Manage reporting processes for endowed funds and current restricted gifts to ensure proper stewardship information is provided to donors to highlight the impact of their philanthropy on an annual basis<br>-Maintain lists of donor recognition societies and execute recognition processes and coordinate with the Director of Annual Giving on society fundraising efforts.<br>-Create recognition and feature stories to be displayed on the Development website.<br>-Create customized donor stewardship plans on an annual basis for top donors in each of the frontline fundraising team's portfolios<br>-Manage all university-wide donor giving society courtesies, impact reporting, and programmatic experiences commensurate with level of giving.<br>-Coordinate with each college-based Director of Development to support college-based giving societies<br>-Manage donor relations touch points for special project and special giving day events.<br>-Assist in analysis and evaluation of stewardship and donor relation programs; recommends new procedures to improve quality, effectiveness, and efficiency.<br>-Other duties as assigned</div> Advancement Services https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48390 2026-09-03T09:01:16-05:00 2026-09-03T09:01:17-05:00 Weight Room Assistant <div>The Weight Room Assistant position in the Athletic Director’s Office is responsible for assisting with operating the weight room for student-athletes; assisting in teaching/training of sound techniques to insure the safety of student-athletes; working with athletic training staff to provide injury rehabilitation; and maintaining the cleanliness of the weight room.</div> Sports Medicine - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48309 2026-08-25T15:32:22-05:00 2026-08-25T15:32:23-05:00 Lecturer <div>The Lecturer of Nursing position is primarily responsible for teaching undergraduate nursing didactic and/or clinical courses, advising BSN students, maintaining involvement in University, College, School, BSN Program, and professional service, and contributing to the nursing body of knowledge through personal and collaborative scholarship.</div> BSN Program - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/32866 2021-11-30T15:12:42-06:00 2023-01-12T11:30:37-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Art and Design <div>The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching courses in Art and Design. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> Art and Design https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47185 2026-05-06T08:52:01-05:00 2026-05-06T08:52:01-05:00 Research Assistant <div>The research assistant position is responsible for data collection and analysis for a research project. The data collection for this research project involves contacting and interviewing potential research participants who are Troy University graduates currently teaching mathematics in middle or high school or aiming to teach mathematics after their graduation. The data analysis involves producing interview transcripts and assist faculty researchers to analyze the data. It also involves some writing tasks, such as preliminary literature review for the research.<br><br></div> Mathematics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48006 2026-07-28T12:03:05-05:00 2026-07-28T12:03:06-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant - Recreation <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant for Recreation duties include:</div><ul><li>Working with other Graduate Assistants on a rotating basis of being “on call” for the facility.</li><li>Ensuring student workers are monitoring workout areas including cleaning equipment and assisting students.</li><li>Monitoring all exercise equipment to ensure that it is operating properly.</li><li>Assisting with the building operations including opening and closing hours, equipment management and additional staff.</li><li>Teaching fitness classes as needed.</li><li>Other duties assigned.</li></ul> Trojan Fitness Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21553 2018-07-09T16:55:32-05:00 2018-11-20T10:34:50-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Accounting The Adjunct Instructor position in Accounting is responsible for teaching entry level Accounting courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. School of Accountancy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46795 2026-03-04T09:04:42-06:00 2026-03-04T09:04:42-06:00 Workship <div>Duties include, but are not limited to, officiating at sporting events through out the semester</div> Intramural Office - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47695 2026-06-23T12:34:37-05:00 2026-06-23T12:34:37-05:00 GIS Data Collection and Resource Mapping <div>employee will help with data collection and GIS database creation</div> Geospatial Informatics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/44556 2025-06-24T10:32:14-05:00 2025-06-24T10:32:15-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Sociology <div>Adjunct faculty members are contract on as needed basic. The Department of Anthropology, Sociology and Criminology are recruiting faculty to teach: 1. The&nbsp;<br>Sociology of Food 2. The Sociology of Cinema 3. Trends in Globalization 4. Gerontology 5. Death and Dying 6. Sociology of Education 7. Sociology of Health,&nbsp;<br>Medical and Illness.</div> Sociology https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47523 2026-06-03T10:17:46-05:00 2026-06-03T10:17:47-05:00 Chemistry Specialist <div>The Chemistry Specialist position is responsible for recruiting high school science teachers to participate in AMSTI/ASIM; implementing a flexible communication system for scheduling labs; preparing activities/labs and supplies for the lab; submission of a weekly itinerary to ASIM Project Director; delivering activities/labs and supplies to participating AMSTI/ASIM teachers as scheduled; providing on-site support and mentoring for new or beginning teachers whenever possible; assisting with laboratory activities, delivering on-site professional development, and providing other training as needed; providing coaching to teachers to help increase their skills and move them to higher performance levels on the Alabama Continuum for Teacher Development based on the Alabama Quality Teaching Standards; coordinating work with the AMSTI site; picking up activities/labs and supplies from participating AMSTI/ASIM teachers in a timely manner; ordering, organizing, and maintaining activities/labs and supplies so they are readily available for classroom use; planning and implementing workshops to train high school science teachers to use AMSTI/ASIM activities/labs; teaching teachers the content background, how to use the activities/labs, and how to effectively lead students through the lab; planning and implementing workshops to train high school science teachers in other areas of science education such as laboratory safety, Science Course of Study, and other topics as needed; working with AMSTI/ASIM teachers and other specialists in developing new lab activities for high school students; attending statewide specialist meetings; participing in the continual improvement and implementation of AMSTI/ASIM; establishing and maintaining open communication with the SDE, project director and teachers; facilitating in a timely preparation and submission of the quarterly financial reports that include proper categorization of expenditures; organizing, properly updating, and promptly submitting Program Report information (visits, class roster, workshop attendance, AMSTI/ASIM inventory, and workshop agendas); communicating regularly regarding use of the AMSTI/ASIM activities/labs and training for AMSTI directors, project directors, system superintendents, principals, and teachers; facilitating the cleaning and maintenance of the AMSTI/ASIM vehicle; collaborating with AMSTI site director and specialist; and assisting AMSTI program with the development and piloting of the new activities/labs as requested.</div> Science in Motion - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48173 2026-08-12T10:47:58-05:00 2026-08-12T10:47:59-05:00 Admissions Counselor <div>College Admissions Counselors are an essential element of the University administrative team. Based on program and location capacity, recruiters build student prospects and new student markets by locating, establishing, assist in developing and implementing recruiting strategies and activities that enhance enrollments.<br>Essential Functions:<br>-Discovers and cultivates prospective student and new market leads.<br>-Recruits prospective students and provides essential information related to admissions requirements and enrollment processes.<br>-Makes vital information available to the community through visits and presentations.<br>-Works collaboratively with University deans, faculty, staff, alumni, and current students to attract new students.<br>-Fosters awareness, promotion, and support of a culture of higher education through outreach.<br>-Assists and supports University initiatives related to recognition and growth.<br>-Assists Enrollment Coordinator with arranging and coordinating faculty and staff visits with community college counselors or other event coordinators.<br><br></div><div>- Strategize on opportunities to enhance Early College efforts in SC territories .<br><br></div><div>-Represent the University at community and outside organization functions including career days, special events and conferences; meet with Principals and South Carolina Independent School Association representatives to organizations to exchange information and answer questions; prepare and deliver presentations regarding programs and services.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div> Support Center - Sumter https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21580 2018-07-09T16:56:53-05:00 2025-09-22T10:32:43-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Operations Management The Adjunct Instructor position in Operations Management is responsible for teaching entry level operations management and management sciences courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Quantitative Methods https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46982 2026-04-08T09:54:50-05:00 2026-04-08T09:54:51-05:00 Warehouse Worker <div>The Warehouse Worker position in AMSTI is responsible for the building and refurbishment of AMSTI modules, maintaining the inventory of materials and supplies for the modules, and physical tasks associated with shipping, receiving, storing and distribution of material.</div> AMSTI - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47892 2026-07-21T08:46:19-05:00 2026-07-21T08:46:20-05:00 Assistant Athletic Trainer <div>The Assistant Athletic Trainer position is responsible for administering programs of injury prevention, injury care and rehabilitation to all student-athletes, with primary daily responsibility for the football program; and proactively ensuring maximum safety to all athletic participants.</div> Athletic Training - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48392 2026-09-03T09:01:32-05:00 2026-09-03T09:01:32-05:00 Switchboard Operator <div>The Switchboard Operator position in Telecommunications is responsible for answering the telephone in an appropriate and professional manner and transferring or directing calls to the correct area.</div> Telecommunications - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47702 2026-06-24T10:24:02-05:00 2026-06-24T10:24:03-05:00 AMSTI Math/Science Specialist <div>The AMSTI Math/Science Specialist position is responsible for providing frequent and on-going professional learning and on-site assistance to K-12 teachers and administrators in Region 11; spending the majority of work time regulated to on-site support, including travel to and from the site; assisting with preparation for professional learning opportunities; assisting schools in effectively using learning teams and common planning time to improve math and science instruction; providing training and guidance to teachers; participation in professional development activities and staff meetings as required by ALSDE; and performing other duties assigned by the AMSTI site director or AMSTI state director.</div> AMSTI - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48327 2026-08-26T13:50:47-05:00 2026-08-26T13:50:48-05:00 Assistant Baseball Coach <div>The Assistant Baseball Coach position is responsible for training, educating and practicing the pitchers for the baseball team; recruiting potential student-athletes to participate on the baseball team; completing workouts for pitchers for the baseball team; and other duties as assigned.</div> Athletics - Baseball - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/36354 2022-11-17T16:02:54-06:00 2022-11-17T16:02:55-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - MSN Program <div><strong>Graduate Nursing Adjunct Instructor</strong><br><br>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Adjunct Instructors may teach no more than 8 semester hours per semester.</div> MSN Program https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47187 2026-05-06T08:58:38-05:00 2026-05-06T08:58:39-05:00 Human Trafficking Internship <div>The Alabama Law Enforcement (ALEA) Internship program provides college and university students with an in-depth, working knowledge of the department. That knowledge is gained though “hands-on” experience in administrative, and in some cases, investigative or patrol settings. The program strives to ensure college or university students will benefit from the experiences gained while participating in the internship program.</div> School of Social Sciences – Sociology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48011 2026-07-28T16:33:01-05:00 2026-07-28T16:33:02-05:00 Lecturer <div>The Lecturer in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training is responsible for teaching graduate-level counseling courses in a CACREP-accredited counselor education program. Responsibilities include course instruction, student advising and mentoring, clinical supervision of practicum and internship students, participation in curriculum development, support for student assessment and remediation processes, service to the department, and contribution to ongoing CACREP accreditation and program evaluation activities.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21555 2018-07-09T16:55:37-05:00 2018-07-09T16:55:38-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Adult Education The Adjunct Instructor position in Adult Education is responsible for teaching related courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Leadership Development and Professional Studies https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46797 2026-03-04T09:04:57-06:00 2026-03-04T09:04:58-06:00 Workship - Learning Center Peer Tutor - STEM <div>This Workship position in Instructional Support Services is a student / peer position responsible for tutoring Troy Campus students and helping present information related to Learning Center services and the tutor's subject concentration(s). Applicants with accounting, finance, economics or computer science minors may be considered, if they also have a Math or Science major. This is not a Graduate Assistantship position nor does it provide tuition assistance.</div> Learning Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48394 2026-09-03T09:03:47-05:00 2026-09-03T09:03:48-05:00 Regional Recruiter - Dallas <div>Troy University Regional Recruiters are an essential element of the University’s Enrollment Management team. This role will be tasked with supporting Troy Campus traditional freshman and transfer student recruitment efforts in a defined geographic region by implementing recruiting strategies and activities that grow the number of students applying to TROY, being admitted to TROY, and ultimately choosing TROY for enrollment. Duties will include constant contact to prospective students and their families as well as establishing positive relationships with high schools, community colleges, and other sources of potential enrollments. Regional recruiters reside in their assigned geographic areas, but will travel to Troy Campus several times a year for training and professional development activities. (All official travel is covered for reimbursement.)<br><br>PLEASE NOTE: Applicants must reside in, or be willing to relocate to, the assigned geographic territory.</div> Admissions - Troy Online https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/45919 2025-11-04T11:44:07-06:00 2025-11-04T11:44:07-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Hospitality, Sport and Tourism Management <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to teach specific courses in the School of Hospitality, Sport and Tourism Management’s undergraduate and graduate programs on an as-needed basis. Adjunct faculty members are issued contracts on a semester/term basis and hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct faculty members are also expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> Hospitality, Sport, and Tourism Management https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47525 2026-06-03T10:20:32-05:00 2026-06-03T10:20:33-05:00 Certified Adaptive Driving Instructor <div>PLEASE NOTE: Position is located in DECATUR, AL<br><br>This position assists the Certified Driving Rehabilitation Specialist (CDRS) in serving consumers in the ADRS Adaptive Driving Program. These duties will include but not be limited to: assisting CDRS in evaluation and training for ADT services, maintaining specialized adaptive equipment and devices related to ADT program for use in the evaluation and treatment of orthopedically, and/or neurologically impaired clients of ADRS, perform scheduled maintenance, service, and minor repair of vehicles and mounting equipment, schedule all service station related work, etc.</div> Human Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48201 2026-08-13T09:02:14-05:00 2026-08-13T09:02:15-05:00 Student Security Officer <div>The Student Security Officer position is responsible for patrolling the grounds of the university by foot and cart to help maintain a safe campus environment.</div> University Police - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21583 2018-07-09T16:57:00-05:00 2023-03-03T09:43:51-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Teacher Education The Adjunct Instructor position in Division of Education is responsible for teaching related courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Department of Teacher Education https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46984 2026-04-08T09:56:34-05:00 2026-04-08T09:56:35-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in the Trojan Fitness Center is responsible for providing assistance in the daily operations of the Trojan Fitness Center.</div> Trojan Fitness Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47921 2026-07-22T09:31:51-05:00 2026-07-22T09:31:51-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position in International Programs is responsible for providing administrative support to the department, including assisting with the Chinese student exchange program.</div> International Programs - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46799 2026-03-04T09:07:28-06:00 2026-03-04T09:07:29-06:00 Workship <div>The workship position in Mathematics is responsible for assisting in math and computer science lab; and tutoring Computer Science students.</div> Computer Science - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47753 2026-07-01T14:28:56-05:00 2026-07-01T14:28:57-05:00 Network Engineer <div>The Network Engineer position in Information Technology is responsible for:</div><ul><li>Designing and/or planning for network enhancements</li><li>Network capacity training</li><li>Assist in building VPN account using FortiAuthenticator</li><li>Maintaining the existing network equipment including but not limited to<ul><li>Routers</li><li>Switches</li><li>Security devices</li><li>Respond to Anomalies</li><li>Work directly with EDL (External Dynamic List) to ward off intruder attempts</li><li>Load-Balancers</li><li>Wireless Controllers</li><li>Access points</li><li>Firewalls</li><li>Monitoring Servers</li></ul></li><li>Monitoring network systems for failure and performance anomalies</li><li>Troubleshooting network issues independently and with network consultants</li><li>End-user support thru Helpdesk Tickets</li><li>Various daily systems reporting and scheduling duties</li><li>Work with Software and Hardware for the following:<ul><li>OPSWAT SafeConnect NAC</li><li>FortiNAC</li><li>BNA (Brocade Network Advisor)</li><li>PRTG (Equipment Monitoring Agent</li><li>FortiAnalyzer</li><li>Panorama Firewall Management Solution</li><li>Aruba Mobility Conductor</li><li>Vectra Security AI</li><li>QRadar Offense Correlation</li><li>Works with external vendors for ISP Connectivity and MPLS Connection Support</li><li>Gets current pricing</li><li>Handles Outages</li><li>Coordination of Scheduled Maintenance Outages</li></ul></li></ul> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48329 2026-08-26T14:30:41-05:00 2026-08-26T14:30:42-05:00 Staff Accountant <div>The Staff Accountant position acts as accounting liaison with the Controller’s Office and other departments and external agencies with respect to financial reporting, tax reporting &amp; compliance, journal entry preparation, audit/reconciliation of accounts, and audit of requests for payment. The position is responsible for preparing and reviewing all types of transactions in compliance with approved budgets and University/department procedures, preparation of appropriate reports as needed for analysis, corresponding with other departments concerning accounting and financial information, and determining proper handling of financial transactions in accordance with Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP) and approving within designated limits, policies or contracts.</div> Controller's Office - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/36356 2022-11-17T16:08:17-06:00 2022-11-17T16:08:18-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - BSN Program <div><strong>Pre-licensure BSN Program Adjunct Instructor </strong><br><br>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Adjunct Instructors may teach no more than 8 semester hours per semester.</div><div>Adjunct postings are intended to serve as a means of accumulating an applicant pool for prospective Adjunct Instructors. Applications will be reviewed as positions become available. Applications may remain active for an extended period of time as the department pulls applicants from the pool to serve in positions on an as-needed basis.</div> BSN Program https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47261 2026-05-12T16:50:30-05:00 2026-05-12T16:50:31-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in Business Programs is responsible for assisting faculty and staff in the Sorrell College of Business with clerical duties as needed.</div> Associate Dean/Administration - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48013 2026-07-28T16:34:05-05:00 2026-07-28T16:34:06-05:00 Lecturer <div>The Lecturer in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training is responsible for teaching graduate-level counseling courses in a CACREP-accredited counselor education program. Responsibilities include course instruction, student advising and mentoring, clinical supervision of practicum and internship students, participation in curriculum development, support for student assessment and remediation processes, service to the department, and contribution to ongoing CACREP accreditation and program evaluation activities.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21557 2018-07-09T16:55:42-05:00 2023-10-19T09:00:12-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Chemistry Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific Chemistry (lecture/lab) courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Chemistry https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48396 2026-09-03T09:05:48-05:00 2026-09-03T09:05:48-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant - MSIR <div>The Center for Eastern and Central European, Russian, and Eurasian Studies (CECERES) at <em>Troy University</em> invites applications for a <strong>Graduate Administrative Assistant</strong> to support the Center’s events, public programming, and visual media efforts. This position is ideal for a graduate student with strong organizational skills and an eye for visual storytelling who is interested in international affairs, academic outreach, and public engagement.</div><div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant will work closely with the Center’s Director and staff to plan, execute, and document lectures, conferences, workshops, and other public-facing activities that advance the Center’s mission.</div><div><strong>About the Center:</strong><br> The Center for Eastern and Central European, Russian, and Eurasian Studies is an interdisciplinary research and outreach center focused on the politics, security, cultures, and societies of Eastern and Central Europe, Russia, and Eurasia. The Center serves as a hub for scholarly research, student engagement, and policy-relevant dialogue, hosting regular public events and supporting academic initiatives that connect Troy University to regional, national, and international audiences.</div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></div><div>Assist in planning, coordinating, and executing Center-sponsored events, including lectures, panels, workshops, conferences, and guest speaker visits.</div><div>Manage event logistics such as room reservations, catering coordination, audiovisual setup, and speaker support.</div><div>Serve as on-site support during events, ensuring smooth operations and professional presentation.</div><div>Photograph and, when appropriate, video-record Center events and activities for archival and promotional use.</div><div>Organize and maintain a digital archive of photos and media assets.</div><div>Assist with post-event follow-up, including compiling attendance information and supporting event summaries.</div><div>Coordinate with the Center’s communications and external relations staff to ensure event materials align with branding and outreach goals.</div> School of Social Sciences – Political Science - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46003 2025-11-17T09:05:21-06:00 2025-11-17T09:05:22-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Political Science <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as needed basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught and are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issues on a semester/term basis</div> Political Science https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47527 2026-06-03T10:20:49-05:00 2026-06-03T10:20:50-05:00 Assistant Materials Specialist <div>The Assistant Materials Specialist position in AMSTI is responsible for assisting with oversight of the operations of the AMSTI Materials center; ensuring that the AIMS data for the region is accurate and up to date; assisting with supervision of workers assigned to the materials center; assisting in providing the materials, supplies, and equipment to AMSTI trained teachers as specified by AMSTI-ALSDE; training workers on correct refurbishment procedures; constructing and refurbishing math and science teaching kits; assisting with coordination of purchasing, inventory, scheduling, and distribution of science and mathematics modules and materials; communicating effectively with teachers about their materials usage and professional learning, based on information provided by AMSTI staff; assisting in organizing the materials center to ensure efficient use of space and storage of materials; assisting to provide reports to the AMSTI Site Directors of AMSTI-ALSDE regarding the teacher and materials database, material costs, distribution schedules, employee assignments, and labor hours, as requested; assisting AMSTI staff with preparation for programs and presentations, and with operation of the material center; assisting with maintaining a safe working environment; attending all required professional learning activities and staff meetings conducted by the ALSDE, unless prior approval for absence is granted by the ALSDE; and performing other duties as assigned by the Materials Manager, AMSTI Site Director, or AMSTI-ALSDE.</div> AMSTI - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48216 2026-08-18T10:24:37-05:00 2026-08-18T10:24:37-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in Chemistry &amp; Physics is responsible for setting up equipment, taking down equipment, and the cleaning of physics labs.</div> Chemistry and Physics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21587 2018-07-09T16:57:10-05:00 2022-06-14T14:34:07-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Clinical The Adjunct Instructor position in Teacher Education is responsible for teaching related courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Department of Certification and Field Experience https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46986 2026-04-08T09:57:41-05:00 2026-04-08T09:57:42-05:00 Archaeological Technician I <div>The Archaeological Technician I position is responsible for working with archaeological collections in the Troy University Archaeological Research Center laboratory. The curation tasks involve processing any newly acquired collections for curation, stabilizing existing collections, and maintaining an up-to-date inventory of all the collections. Primary duties include transferring artifacts into new bags and boxes that meet the curation standard. This position will also assist the anthropology faculty in ensuring our collections meet federal guidelines related to the Native American Graves Repatriation and Protection Act (NAGPRA).</div> Archaeological Research Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47926 2026-07-22T10:29:54-05:00 2026-07-22T10:29:55-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Interpreter Training position in the College of Education is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in clinical mental health counseling and other counseling specialties; pursuing a scholarship and research agenda; service on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community; advising graduate students; and supervising Practicum and Internship students.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46869 2026-03-18T08:18:51-05:00 2026-03-18T08:18:51-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer in Counselor Education is a non tenure track instructional faculty position with primary responsibility for teaching graduate level coursework in the Clinical Mental Health Counseling program. The position supports delivery of the required 60 hour CACREP accredited curriculum and contributes to program quality, continuity, and compliance with accreditation standards.</div><div>Primary responsibilities include teaching graduate courses in research, assessment, counseling theories, facilitation skills for individuals and groups, behavior pathology and diagnosis and treatment, as well as supervision of practicum and internship experiences. In accordance with University policy for lecturer appointments, the position also includes academic advisement, availability to students during scheduled office hours, participation in program and University service activities, engagement in ongoing professional development and appropriate scholarly activity, and the development and maintenance of professional and community partnerships relevant to counselor preparation.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47770 2026-07-06T10:54:01-05:00 2026-07-06T10:54:02-05:00 Intramural Official <div>The Intramural Official position in the Intramural Office is responsible for assisting with officating intramural activities and field maintenance.</div> Intramural Office - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48335 2026-08-27T11:02:11-05:00 2026-08-27T11:02:11-05:00 Workship - Costume Assistant <div>The Workship position in the Department of Theatre and Dance is responsible for assisting the Costume Design faculty with research, design, construction of costumes, fitting costumes, cleaning and organizing costumes and managing the costume shop.</div> Theatre & Dance - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/40350 2024-03-19T08:14:24-05:00 2024-07-16T14:34:52-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Mathematics https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47283 2026-05-14T12:24:41-05:00 2026-05-14T12:24:42-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position for the Professional Lab Experience (Office of Certification &amp; Field Experiences), within the College of Education, is responsible for, but not limited to the following: assisting with all administrative duties, assisting students with support for edTPA completion; data entry, assisting with reports and providing research information upon request.</div> Department of Certification and Field Experience - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48056 2026-08-04T11:42:59-05:00 2026-08-04T11:43:00-05:00 Programmer Analyst I <div>The Programmer Analyst I position in Information Technology is responsible for programming, implementing, and maintaining computer programs, query language, and user screens to better facilitate daily operations and effective administrative computing for the University; and providing technical support to end-users which includes problem solving, ad-hoc reporting, creating technical documentation, and analysis of application software processes.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21559 2018-07-09T16:55:49-05:00 2021-08-13T13:16:04-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Computer Science Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Computer Science https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47928 2026-07-22T10:31:53-05:00 2026-07-22T10:31:54-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor position in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training is a tenure-track faculty position for Clinical Mental Health Counseling. This position is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in the clinical mental health program and core counseling courses within the specific area of expertise; pursuit of a scholarship and research agenda; service on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community. This position also includes administrative responsibilities such as advising graduate students and supervising Practicum and Internship students, scheduling counseling courses, recruiting students for the program, proctoring and grading comprehensive examinations, attending faculty meetings, and attending required region meetings for faculty.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48402 2026-09-03T16:53:45-05:00 2026-09-03T16:53:45-05:00 Senior Educational Technology Administrator <div>The Senior Educational Technology Administrator serves as an administrator for the University's Canvas Learning Management System (LMS), ensuring its reliability, security, availability, and optimal performance to support teaching and learning. This position provides advanced technical support by troubleshooting and resolving complex Canvas-related issues for faculty, staff, students, and administrators while maintaining a high level of customer service in a fast-paced support environment. Manages and resolves support requests through the TeamDynamix ticketing system, responds to escalated support cases referred by Instructure Support, including Canvas chat sessions and institutional support tickets requiring administrative intervention, and performs remote troubleshooting sessions using approved remote support software. This position is responsible for creating Canvas organizations used for university communications, faculty development, student engagement, training initiatives, and other institutional purposes. The Senior Administrator also develops, updates, and maintains online student training courses designed to orient first-time Canvas users and promote successful navigation and utilization of the University's learning management system.<br><br></div><div>The Senior Systems Administrator maintains, and supports educational technology applications that integrate with Canvas, including Turnitin Plagiarism Detection, Respondus LockDown Browser and Monitor, Respondus 4.0 Test Bank, NetTutor Online Tutoring, Microsoft Teams, Camtasia, Watermarks’ Student Learning and Licensure and other Learning Tools Interoperability (LTI) applications and third-party instructional technologies, such as- Pearson and McGraw-Hill. The position develops and maintains comprehensive technical documentation, standard operating procedures, user guides, and TeamDynamix Knowledge Base articles to support self-service resources and improve the overall user experience.<br><br></div><div>This position requires evening and weekend work to provide technical support to end users, perform system maintenance, software upgrades, and emergency troubleshooting.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46005 2025-11-17T09:05:33-06:00 2025-11-17T09:05:34-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Public Administration <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as needed basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught and are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issues on a semester/term basis&nbsp;</div> Political Science https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47574 2026-06-08T15:24:29-05:00 2026-06-08T15:24:30-05:00 Graduate Research Fellow (GAAN) <div>The Graduate Research (GAAN) Fellow position in Biology is responsible for graduate student research leading to an M.S. (thesis track) in Environmental and Biological Sciences at Troy University, including all expectations of professional development, mentorship, and activities required by the GAAN grant funded by the Department of Education.</div> Biology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48236 2026-08-18T16:47:38-05:00 2026-08-18T16:47:39-05:00 IT Specialist I <div>The Information Technology Specialist I position in Information Technology is responsible for installing, troubleshooting, repairing and maintaining hardware; providing advanced support for a wide variety of software applications; and completing helpdesk requests in a timely manner in a high-paced environment.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21589 2018-07-09T16:57:15-05:00 2022-07-28T11:23:13-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Mathematics Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Mathematics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47048 2026-04-20T15:57:49-05:00 2026-04-20T15:57:50-05:00 Project Advisor <div>The Project Advisor position for Student Support Services is responsible for serving as an academic advisor to program participants; administering and evaluating academic and needs survey assessments; creating and maintaining Individual Academic and Service Plans (IASP) on assigned participants; providing individual and group coaching in writing, math, and/or study skills; assisting participants with graduate/professional school planning; developing and conducting student development/academic/graduation workshops; accompanying program participants to cultural events; attending professional development training; and other duties as assigned by the Project Coordinator. Travel will be required when needed.</div> Student Support Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21562 2018-07-09T16:55:59-05:00 2018-07-09T16:56:00-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Modern Languages and Classics The Adjunct Instructor position in Modern Languages and Classics is responsible for teaching courses in foreign languages. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. World Languages and Cultures https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46902 2026-03-23T12:32:41-05:00 2026-03-23T12:32:41-05:00 Lecturer/Professor of Practice/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The <strong>Scenic Design &amp; Technolog</strong>y faculty position is a full-time position hired on a 10-month renewable contract. The open-rank posting allows for for authentic consideration of candidates’ unique strengths and potential to serve in the role of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, Lecturer, or Professor of Practice. <br><br>The <strong>Scenic Design &amp; Technology</strong> full-time faculty position is responsible for oversight of scenic design and technology for all productions; teaching courses in design, technology, technical theatre, and general theatre; producing quality theatrical scenery and scenic elements that complement and support theatre and dance productions and presentations; working closely with the Technical Director and Scene Shop Manager to construct, fabricate, and finish scenic elements to full completion within production timelines and standards; assisting with oversight of inventory, acquisition, organization, management, repair, and installation of technology and tools in the scenic area; supervising and training student leaders and crews in scenic area(s); working with other faculty to develop curriculum and projects aimed specifically to students with goals and interests in the field of Design/Technology/Management; providing a focus on innovating and advancing ideas and practices in theatrical design and technology; advising and mentoring students; contributing to the artistic and intellectual growth of the Department, College and University; participation in the work of faculty and the Department; working within professional networks and organizations beyond the University; and continuing to develop their own artistry and gain experience in the field.</div> Theatre & Dance - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47772 2026-07-06T10:55:58-05:00 2026-07-06T10:55:59-05:00 Usher <div>The Usher position for the Davis Theatre is responsible for assisting Theatre staff with ushering at children shows and other theatre events.</div> Davis Theatre - Montgomery https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48351 2026-08-27T16:08:15-05:00 2026-08-27T16:08:16-05:00 Band Event Staff - Office <div>Work in Band Office as needed</div> Band - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/42508 2024-10-28T09:45:49-05:00 2025-07-29T12:57:27-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Leadership Institute <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> Leadership Institute https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47305 2026-05-15T09:36:02-05:00 2026-05-15T09:36:03-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position for the Office of Certification and Field Experience, within the College of Education, is responsible for assisting with a variety of clerical and administrative duties including but not limited to data entry, reports and research; and assisting with the implementation and training of undergraduate students for the edTPA process.</div> Department of Certification and Field Experience - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48058 2026-08-04T11:43:15-05:00 2026-08-04T11:43:15-05:00 IT Facility Manager <div>The IT Facility Manager position in Information Technology is responsible for maintaining and servicing the IT facility including, but not limited to the primary building, annex, John Lewis Hall datacenter, and IT datacenter. This includes routine maintenance of systems including: Fire alarm, fire suppression system, security alarm system, fob access system, CCTV, generator, transfer switch, UPS, etc. This position requires organization to ensure systems are maintained, inspected, and services in an appropriate time frame to ensure operations of the IT department continue without interruption. This position needs to report updates and issues to key personnel to make sure they are aware of the status of systems and make sure they are aware of issues and ensuring they are resolved in a timely manner. The IT Facility Manager is responsible for handling all work orders for the facilities and escorting Physical Plant through secure areas. This position is also responsible for maintaining tape back ups for critical systems ensuring back ups are pulled, logged, and stored appropriately. Other duties as assigned.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47144 2026-04-28T16:38:10-05:00 2026-04-28T16:38:11-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Assistant position for the Sorrell College of Business will be responsible for various duties in support the of the Dean's Office. This includes: social media communications, website support, and other general support duties needed by the Sorrell College. This person will report directly to the Dean's Office.</div> Dean's Office - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47949 2026-07-23T11:30:02-05:00 2026-07-23T11:30:03-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Assistant/Associate Professor position in the Sorrell College of Business is a full-time, tenure-track faculty appointment on a ten-month contract, beginning August 1, 2027.<br><br>The candidate will teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in marketing, entrepreneurship, or related areas. Candidates must possess appropriate academic qualifications in marketing, entrepreneurship, or a closely related field. Instruction will be delivered primarily on the Troy Campus, with regular online teaching responsibilities.<br><br>In addition to teaching, the candidate will be expected to collaborate with the Troy University IDEA Bank Student Entrepreneurship Center; engage in scholarly research and maintain faculty qualifications consistent with AACSB standards; advise students; and provide service to the department, college, university, profession, and community.</div> School of Creative Enterprise and Market Systems - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21543 2018-07-09T16:55:06-05:00 2023-11-06T16:03:00-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Risk Management Insurance The Adjunct Instructor position in Risk Management Insurance is responsible for teaching Principles of Insurance or other undergraduate RMI courses.  Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Risk Management Insurance https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46302 2026-01-06T14:34:41-06:00 2026-01-06T14:34:42-06:00 Adjunct Faculty <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to teach specific science and engineering courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> Chemistry and Physics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47591 2026-06-10T11:43:41-05:00 2026-06-10T11:43:42-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in the CMMS is responsible for:</div><ul><li>Transporting materials and deliveries.</li><li>Maintaining cleanliness and organizing shared laboratory spaces.</li><li>Assisting with facility tours, demonstrations, and special events as needed.</li><li>Printing, organizing, and updating Safety Data Sheets (SDS) for all laboratories.</li><li>Assisting with additional tasks as assigned to support CMMS operations and maintain a safe working environment.</li></ul> Chemistry and Physics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48255 2026-08-19T11:59:23-05:00 2026-08-19T11:59:24-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Interpreter Training position in the College of Education is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in clinical mental health counseling and other counseling specialties; pursuing a scholarship and research agenda; service on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community; advising graduate students; and supervising Practicum and Internship students.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21631 2018-07-09T16:59:00-05:00 2025-09-04T11:21:31-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Leadership Development Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Leadership Development https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48060 2026-08-04T11:47:03-05:00 2026-08-04T11:47:03-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in the office of Human Resources is responsible for providing administrative office support to the department.</div> Human Resources - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21564 2018-07-09T16:56:05-05:00 2022-12-14T13:59:47-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Human Resource Management Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Human Resource Management https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46940 2026-03-30T15:30:31-05:00 2026-03-30T15:30:32-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Assistant Professor/Associate Professor position in the College of Education is a tenure-track faculty role within the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training. This position also serves as the Coordinator of Rehabilitation, providing leadership and oversight for the rehabilitation counseling program. The role presents an opportunity to contribute to a dynamic and growing counseling program, preparing the next generation of professionals through teaching, mentorship, research, and program coordination. Faculty members in this role are responsible for teaching online graduate courses in rehabilitation and clinical mental health counseling, coordinating and supporting the rehabilitation counseling program, conducting and publishing scholarly research, and engaging in service to the department, university, and broader professional community.<br><br>Key responsibilities include providing academic advising and mentorship to graduate students, supervising practicum and internship students, and managing essential administrative duties such as course scheduling, student recruitment, maintaining office hours, and participating in faculty meetings. Faculty are also expected to proctor and grade comprehensive examinations, attend regional faculty meetings, and actively contribute to the advancement of CACREP-accredited programs.<br><br>This role is well-suited for individuals who are passionate about counselor education and committed to professional excellence. The position offers a unique opportunity to shape the future of the counseling profession through high-quality instruction, meaningful mentorship, and impactful research. Candidates who are dedicated to fostering student success and advancing the field of counseling are encouraged to apply.</div> Department of C R I T - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47774 2026-07-06T10:58:38-05:00 2026-07-06T10:58:39-05:00 Assistive Technology Specialist <div>Position located in <strong>Huntsville, AL</strong></div><ul><li>Serves as liaison between Department of Rehabilitation and school systems to handle student assistive technology needs.</li><li>Provides assistive technology consultation and assessment to students.</li><li>Develops a written assistive technology report, including specifications on recommend AT intervention.</li><li>Document work in case management databases, timesheets, and paper files.</li><li>Works with school staff, ADRS counselors, and when necessary rehab engineers, to implement the assistive technology recommendations to meet the student’s needs. Provides set-up, fitting, training, and technical support on AT devices.</li><li>Participates in quality improvement and quality assurance activities, and provides guidance, information, and assistance on assistive technology services.</li><li>Markets assistive technology services to schools and other agencies.</li><li>Create and maintains a high performance environment characterized by positive leadership and strong team orientation.</li><li>Maintains knowledge of current trends and development in the field by reading appropriate books, journals, and other literature and attending related seminars and conferences to obtain pertinent new knowledge to performance of job responsibilities.</li></ul> Human Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48364 2026-08-31T08:46:00-05:00 2026-08-31T08:46:00-05:00 College of Education Communication Coordinator <div>The Communication Coordinator for the College of Education and Behavioral Sciences works closely with the Dean, department chairs, faculty, and other stakeholders <strong>under the direction of the Office of University Relations</strong> to develop and distribute strategic communications that advance public awareness of the College’s mission, programs, and impact.</div><div><br>This position supports the College’s communications and media relations efforts by assisting with media inquiries, helping pitch faculty expertise and College initiatives, and coordinating with the University Relations office to generate positive external media coverage. The Communication Coordinator also assists with creating and maintaining content for the College’s website and social media channels and serves as a liaison with the Marketing and Communications office to facilitate requests and ensure compliance with University brand guidelines.</div><div><br><strong>Key Responsibilities and Deliverables</strong></div><div><br>The Communication Coordinator will focus on the following core areas:</div><div><br><strong>Writing and Content Creation</strong></div><ul><li>Write news releases, feature stories, web content, and other communications materials highlighting faculty, students, programs, and initiatives</li><li>Edit content for clarity, accuracy, tone, and Associated Press style</li><li>Assist with internal and external communications as needed</li></ul><div><br><strong>Social Media, Web, and Marketing Support</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with developing and managing content for the College’s social media channels in alignment with University strategy</li><li>Create engaging digital content to support recruitment, outreach, and reputation-building efforts</li><li>Update and maintain College web pages using the University’s content management system</li><li>Coordinate with the University’s Marketing and Communications office on campaigns, requests, and brand compliance</li></ul><div><br><strong>Media Relations and Public Relations</strong></div><ul><li>Assist with media relations efforts, including responding to inquiries and coordinating interviews</li><li>Support efforts to pitch faculty experts, research, and College initiatives to local, regional, and national media</li><li>Assist with media monitoring and reporting</li><li>Provide basic event coverage, including photography and limited video support as needed</li></ul> University Relations - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/43544 2025-03-05T12:08:35-06:00 2025-03-05T12:08:35-06:00 Adjunct Instructor <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> Computer Science - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47334 2026-05-19T09:33:02-05:00 2026-05-19T09:33:03-05:00 Academic Services Associate <div>The Academic Services Associate (ASA) position for TROY Online Academic Services is responsible for:<br>• Assisting advisees with the planning and registering of classes.<br>• Keeping students on track and focusing on the retention of advisees<br>• Focusing on student engagement<br>• Working daily CRM Alerts and Tasks related to student progression<br>• Coordinate with ID and other areas on special projects</div> Advisement - Troy Online https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/26735 2019-10-21T15:40:44-05:00 2023-03-14T08:52:32-05:00 Adjunct Faculty - Global Leadership The Adjunct Faculty position for Global Leadership is responsible for teaching doctoral level courses ranging from content (e.g., global leadership and organizational management) to research methods (e.g., introduction to research, research design). Courses will be assigned based on the specific credentials that are within the faculty member's educational coursework and professional background.  This position is also responsible for developing curriculum, course materials, video lectures, labs, and presentations as assigned; and participating in program and course level learning assessments.  This position may be expected to serve on dissertation committees, as assigned by the program director. \r\n\r\nOther responsibilities: \r\n- Preparation of interactive presentations for quality face-to-face and online teaching \r\n- Respond to student inquiries in a timely manner \r\n- Provision of substantive and ongoing feedback to students \r\n- Maintenance and enhancement of the quality of teaching in the program \r\n- Attendance at adjunct faculty meetings Department of Leadership, Development and Professional Studies - Global Campus https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47178 2026-05-06T08:39:59-05:00 2026-05-06T08:39:59-05:00 Assistant Professor <div>Troy University invites applications for a full time, 10-month renewable contract, tenure track position as Assistant Professor in History. The position is responsible for teaching introductory courses in World History and upper division (and potentially graduate) courses on topics relevant to the incumbent's research interests. The department seeks an instructor who specializes in History of early modern to modern Britain and/or France, ideally with some degree of specialization in the history of the Middle East and/or history of Africa. The teaching load will be four courses per semester. These will be taught in class and potentially online. This position is expected to begin in August 2023.</div> History - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47957 2026-07-23T14:36:15-05:00 2026-07-23T14:36:16-05:00 Workship <div>The workship position will be responsible for assisting the director of the Arboretum<br>in maintaining/enhancing the grounds. Possible job duties include grass mowing, trail<br>clearing, removal of invasive species, and planting of native vegetation.</div> Biology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21548 2018-07-09T16:55:19-05:00 2021-03-22T09:17:16-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Management The Adjunct Instructor position in Management is responsible for teaching management and human resource management courses.\r\nAdjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Management https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46647 2026-02-10T09:52:39-06:00 2026-02-10T09:52:39-06:00 Assistant Professor <div>The School of Social Sciences at Troy University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Political Science to teach courses in American Politics. The School of Social Sciences houses a vibrant community of scholars in the fields of Anthropology, Criminology, Sociology, Legal Studies, and Political Science. The anticipated start date is August 2026.</div><div>We seek candidates with a Ph.D. in Political Science or Government to support the growth and development of our Political Science major and associated student organizations. Doctoral candidates who are ABD and near graduation will also be considered.<br><br></div><div>If hired, the candidate will be responsible for teaching 12 credit hours per semester (4/4 teaching load) in a combination of face-to-face and online undergraduate courses focused on American national government, legislative politics, executive politics and bureaucracy, political methodology, and other advanced subjects within their expertise. We highly encourage applicants whose research focuses on any of the following areas, including, but not limited to: legislative politics, campaigns and elections, executive politics, and the separation of powers. The successful candidate will maintain an active research agenda, mentor and advise students, and provide service to the department, college, university, and community. The successful candidate will also support the growth of the Political Science major and involve undergraduate students in research opportunities</div> School of Social Sciences – Political Science - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47622 2026-06-11T10:22:07-05:00 2026-06-11T10:22:08-05:00 Academic Program Specialist <div>The Academic Program Specialist provides administrative support and manages a variety of academic and departmental processes for the School of Management. The position reports to the School Director. Duties and responsibilities include: general office duties; internship and recruiting responsibilities and duties; event planning activities and duties; student support; scholarship assistance; schedule, coordinate, and plan meetings; assist with faculty meetings; responsible for all recordkeeping and filing of required contracts and essential recordkeeping information; assist faculty as needed; and assist visitors to the School.</div> School of Management - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48266 2026-08-20T12:44:00-05:00 2026-08-20T12:44:00-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in International Programs is responsible for assisting with the process of admitting and enrolling new international students; assisting international recruitment and admission efforts; general department support; and assisting with application processing, expediting issues, printing, filling, research, orientation assistant, language support on emails and phone.</div> International Programs - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48118 2026-08-06T11:58:35-05:00 2026-08-06T11:58:35-05:00 Helpdesk Operator <div>The Helpdesk Operator position in Information Technology is responsible for answering IT Helpdesk phone calls; providing basic troubleshooting for computer problems covered in training; directing callers to online knowledge base, and other resources, for additional support when applicable; assisting callers in creating helpdesk accounts, submitting tickets and utilizing support history tools; submitting, reviewing, updating, and closing tickets for callers as needed; directing callers to appropriate further assistance if issue is not supported by IT Helpdesk; rotating and logging backup tapes, as covered in training; and other additional duties as assigned.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21566 2018-07-09T16:56:11-05:00 2022-06-14T10:10:47-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Social Work The Adjunct Instructor position in Social Work is responsible for teaching across a curriculum to include HBSE I and II, Social Policy, and Social Work Methods; and may be asked to develop elective classes based on the areas of expertise.\r\nAdjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Social Work https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46966 2026-04-07T11:17:49-05:00 2026-04-07T11:17:50-05:00 Assistant Professor <div>The Department of Computer Science at Troy University invites applications for a 10-month tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Computer Science and Cybersecurity, beginning in August 2026. The department currently has nine full-time faculty members and offers BS programs in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, and Applied Computer Science, as well as an MS program in Computer Science.</div> Computer Science - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47777 2026-07-06T11:04:32-05:00 2026-07-06T11:04:32-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position in the College of Education is responsible for assisting faculty with teaching and research related activities such as data entry, literature searches, and other research/administrative work.</div> Department of C R I T - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48372 2026-08-31T11:32:09-05:00 2026-08-31T11:32:10-05:00 University Archivist <div>The University Archivist position in the Library is a professional staff position and is responsible for serving as a senior advisor to university leadership in the development of the archives, and providing expertise in accepted standards and best practices of archival administration.</div> Library - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/44551 2025-06-24T10:27:27-05:00 2025-09-18T13:32:18-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Criminal Justice <div>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as needed basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught and are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issues on a semester/term basis</div> Criminal Justice https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47476 2026-06-01T09:41:23-05:00 2026-06-01T09:41:23-05:00 Assistant Professor <div>This position is primarily responsible for teaching graduate courses in nursing and advising students in the MSN and DNP programs. Also, maintain full faculty involvement in University, College, School, and professional service. Contribute to the nursing body of knowledge through personal and collaborative scholarship. Effective leadership skills and the ability to work collegially in a group of dedicated graduate faculty is required. Assistant/Associate/Professor positions will be required to teach 12 semester hours per semester (or 24 semester hours per AY).</div> MSN Program - Montgomery https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/28896 2020-08-24T14:37:06-05:00 2023-07-27T13:05:06-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Undergraduate Rehabilitation The Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Interpreter Training is seeking adjunct faculty to teach in the undergraduate Rehabilitation and Disability Studies program located at the Troy Campus, but may include other locations. This position is responsible for teaching undergraduate students in an interactive environment.  Adjunct instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding coursework; are employed to provide specific courses on an as needed basis; and are responsible for the management of assigned courses. Division of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47181 2026-05-06T08:44:18-05:00 2026-05-06T08:44:19-05:00 Patrolman <div>The Patrolman position in University Police is responsible for serving as a police officer by managing the safety and security of students, faculty, staff, visitors and property at the University; and working a specified shift with other officers to patrol all areas of the campus.</div> University Police - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47963 2026-07-24T08:31:48-05:00 2026-07-24T08:31:49-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor position in the Psychology Program in the College of Education and Behavioral Sciences is a 10-month appointment at Troy University’s Troy Campus. This position is responsible for: teaching courses in Forensic Psychology and/or other graduate and undergraduate psychology courses; advising and mentoring students; developing a research agenda; providing service to the community, profession, department, college, and university; and performing other duties as assigned by the department chair. Faculty rank will be dependent on experience and training.</div> Department of Psychology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21550 2018-07-09T16:55:25-05:00 2018-07-09T16:55:26-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Finance The Adjunct Instructor position in Finance is responsible for teaching beginning level Finance courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Finance https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46792 2026-03-04T09:02:07-06:00 2026-03-04T09:02:07-06:00 Workship - Natural Science Center Tutor <div>The Workship position in the Natural Science Center is a student worker position that is responsible for tutoring Troy University students in Math and Science courses.</div> Natural Science Center https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47638 2026-06-11T13:55:02-05:00 2026-06-11T13:55:03-05:00 Lecturer of Music Industry-Live Sound and Event Production <div>Troy University is seeking an energetic and experienced music industry professional to join the faculty of the John M. Long School of Music faculty. The Music Industry program is well-established, and includes multiple, music focused undergraduate majors as well as a graduate degree option through the MBA- Music Industry Emphasis offered in collaboration with the Sorrell College of Business.</div><div>The successful candidate will teach courses in live sound, concert production, and related areas while providing technical and production leadership for the American Popular Music Ensemble (POPulus) and other Music Industry program events. This position combines classroom instruction with hands-on experiential learning through real-world concert production and student technical training.</div><div>Responsibilities include teaching core undergraduate music industry courses, mentoring student production crews, coordinating production logistics for concerts and recruitment events within the School of Music, and serving as lead audio engineer for POPulus performances and other program concerts including Bands, choirs, Jazz Ensemble, and chamber groups. This role will help ensure that program concerts and events are produced at professional industry standards while serving as meaningful training environments for students preparing for careers in live sound, touring, concert production, and event technology; provide leadership in the planning, coordination, and maintenance of live production systems and infrastructure supporting Music Industry program performances and events; mentor student engineers and technical crews while helping students develop the skills, professionalism, and industry awareness necessary for careers in the live entertainment industry.</div><div>Additional responsibilities may include assisting with music industry program development, supporting student recruitment and outreach activities, mentoring student production teams, and contributing to experiential learning opportunities that connect classroom instruction with real world production environments.<br><br></div><div>The start date for the position is August 1, 2026. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled.<br><br><strong>Required Documents</strong></div><div>1. Cover Letter</div><div>2. List of three References</div><div>3. Curriculum Vitae</div><div>4. Unofficial Transcripts</div><div>5. A Portfolio including three examples of professional work related to live sound, concert production, or audio engineering. Please upload a text file with links only.</div> Music - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48274 2026-08-21T11:07:15-05:00 2026-08-21T11:07:15-05:00 Tutor <div>The Tutor position in International Programs is responsible for providing tutoring services to students in the public school system.</div> International Programs - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47516 2026-06-02T13:13:32-05:00 2026-06-02T13:13:32-05:00 ID Office Clerk <div>The Trojan ID Office Clerk position in Student Financial Services is responsible for creating and printing ID cards for students, faculty, and staff. This position also facilitates the sale of commuter meal plans and adds Trojan Cash to ID cards.</div> Student Financial Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48151 2026-08-07T18:24:06-05:00 2026-08-07T18:24:06-05:00 Assistant Athletic Director/Director for Marketing and Fan Engagement <div>The Assistant Athletics Director of Marketing and Fan Engagement position is responsible for planning marketing leadership strategies; and managing all areas of the marketing of all Athletic Events.</div> Athletic Promotions - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21574 2018-07-09T16:56:38-05:00 2024-08-01T14:41:18-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - English The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching courses in English. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. English https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46978 2026-04-08T09:52:27-05:00 2026-04-08T09:52:27-05:00 Bus Driver <div>The Bus Driver position is responsible for driving buses for various shuttle routes on campus and group trips off campus.</div> Student Services - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47811 2026-07-10T11:41:00-05:00 2026-07-10T11:41:01-05:00 IT Specialist II <div>The Information Technology Specialist II position in Information Technology is responsible for installing, troubleshooting, repairing and maintaining hardware; providing advanced support for a wide variety of software applications; and completing helpdesk requests in a timely manner in a fast-paced environment.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48381 2026-09-02T09:30:44-05:00 2026-09-02T09:30:44-05:00 Lab Assistant <div>The primary focus of this project is to construct and implement a classification system for multiple STEM laboratories' equipment and machines, inventory consumable and reusable laboratory equipment, design a laboratory set-up manual for STEM teaching assistants, and test/ edit reserve online STEM labs.</div> Chemistry and Physics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/44553 2025-06-24T10:29:10-05:00 2025-06-24T10:29:11-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Philosophy <div>The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching courses including Introduction to Philosophy, Ethics and the Modern World, Introduction to Political Philosophy, Introduction to Logic, Critical Thinking, Western Philosophy, Non Western Philosophy, Applied Ethics, and Philosophy of Religion. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> Philosophy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48295 2026-08-25T08:15:02-05:00 2026-08-25T08:15:03-05:00 Senior Director of Institutional Research, Planning & Effectiveness <div>The Director of Institutional Research, Planning &amp; Effectiveness position typically oversees institutional effectiveness, assessment, accreditation, and data-driven decision-making across the university. The core responsibilities are:</div><div>1. Institutional Effectiveness &amp; Assessment</div><ul><li>Develop and maintain the institution's comprehensive effectiveness framework</li><li>Coordinate assessment of student learning outcomes (SLOs) across all academic programs</li><li>Oversee program-level assessment plans and results</li><li>Aggregate assessment data and report findings to leadership and accreditors</li><li>Help faculty and departments use assessment results for continuous improvement</li><li>Ensure alignment between institutional mission, goals, and assessment activities</li></ul><div>2. Accreditation &amp; Compliance</div><ul><li>Serve as liaison to regional and specialized accreditors</li><li>Prepare self-study reports and accreditation documentation</li><li>Coordinate institutional response to accreditation recommendations</li><li>Track compliance with accreditation standards</li><li>Manage accreditation timelines and evidence collection</li><li>Prepare for accreditation visits</li></ul><div>3. Strategic Planning</div><ul><li>Develop and maintain the institution's strategic plan</li><li>Align strategic goals with mission and accreditation standards</li><li>Coordinate strategic planning process with all stakeholders</li><li>Monitor progress on strategic initiatives</li><li>Publish annual strategic plan updates and progress reports</li><li>Connect strategic goals to budget and resource allocation</li></ul><div>4. Institutional Research &amp; Analytics</div><ul><li>Collect, analyze, and report institutional data</li><li>Produce regular dashboards and reports (enrollment, retention, graduation, demographics, financial, etc.)</li><li>Conduct ad hoc research and analysis for decision-makers</li><li>Maintain data integrity and institutional databases</li><li>Benchmark against peer institutions</li><li>Publish fact books and data summaries</li></ul><div>5. Program Review &amp; Evaluation</div><ul><li>Develop and oversee program review process (academic and administrative)</li><li>Coordinate annual or periodic reviews of all programs</li><li>Ensure reviews include student learning outcomes, enrollment, retention, costs</li><li>Help programs develop improvement plans based on review findings</li><li>Track implementation of improvement recommendations</li><li>Report program review results to leadership</li></ul><div>6. Learning Outcomes &amp; Curriculum Alignment</div><ul><li>Develop institution-wide general education learning outcomes</li><li>Map program-level outcomes to institutional outcomes</li><li>Coordinate assessment of general education across disciplines</li><li>Work with faculty on outcomes development and rubric creation</li><li>Help departments document student achievement of learning outcomes</li><li>Use outcome data to inform curriculum improvements</li></ul><div>7. Data &amp; Reporting Systems</div><ul><li>Oversee institutional data warehouse or systems</li><li>Ensure accurate, timely data collection and reporting</li><li>Provide training on data tools and dashboards</li><li>Maintain institutional research databases</li><li>Coordinate with IT on data systems and security</li><li>Publish regular reports (enrollment, retention, graduation, demographics, etc.)</li></ul><div>8. Stakeholder Communication</div><ul><li>Present data and findings to Board of Trustees</li><li>Brief senior leadership on institutional performance</li><li>Support department chairs with assessment and program review</li><li>Communicate effectiveness results to faculty and staff</li><li>Respond to data requests from various departments</li><li>Publish annual effectiveness reports</li></ul><div>9. Quality Assurance &amp; Continuous Improvement</div><ul><li>Monitor key performance indicators (KPIs)</li><li>Identify trends and areas for improvement</li><li>Support departments in implementing evidence-based changes</li><li>Track whether improvement initiatives are working</li><li>Conduct surveys (student satisfaction, employee engagement, etc.)</li><li>Use data to support institutional decision-making</li></ul><div>10. Budget &amp; Resource Alignment</div><ul><li>Analyze resource allocation in relation to outcomes</li><li>Support evidence-based budgeting</li><li>Help justify resource requests with assessment data</li><li>Track ROI on institutional investments</li><li>Coordinate with CFO on budget decisions informed by effectiveness data</li></ul><div>11. Staff Leadership &amp; Team Management</div><ul><li>Supervise IR/Assessment staff</li><li>Manage IRPE office budget and operations</li><li>Provide professional development for team</li><li>Coordinate with other departments (Registrar, Admissions, Finance, etc.)</li><li>Build collaborative relationships across campus</li></ul><div>12. Professional Development &amp; Best Practices</div><ul><li>Stay current on institutional effectiveness trends and standards</li><li>Attend professional conferences (AIR, ACUHO, regional associations)</li><li>Share best practices with peers</li><li>Implement new assessment methods and tools</li><li>Mentor faculty and staff on assessment design</li></ul><div>Key Competencies for the Director</div><ul><li>Data analysis and interpretation</li><li>Strong writing and presentation skills</li><li>Leadership and collaboration</li><li>Knowledge of accreditation standards</li><li>Project management</li><li>Educational assessment expertise</li><li>Strategic thinking</li><li>Attention to detail</li></ul> Institutional Research Planning and Effectiveness - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/30116 2021-03-08T09:12:02-06:00 2022-12-01T11:06:17-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Applied Behavior Analysis Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Department of Psychology https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47184 2026-05-06T08:49:09-05:00 2026-05-06T08:49:10-05:00 Postdoctoral Associate <div>Troy University invites applications for a Postdoctoral Research Associate position hosted in the College of Science and Engineering. We are seeking a highly motivated and skilled researcher with a strong background in semiconductor plasmonics, energy harvesting devices, photonics and computational electromagnetics.</div><div><strong>Key Responsibilities:<br></strong><br></div><ul><li>Conduct independent and collaborative research in Photonics, semiconductor plasmonics and energy harvesting technologies.</li><li>Establish and manage a new optoelectronics laboratory, including equipment setup and operations.</li><li>Contribute to and support grant writing efforts, including preparation of proposals and reports.</li><li>Supervise and mentor undergraduate and graduate student researchers in relevant projects.</li><li>Teach one introductory course in Electrical and Electronic Engineering per semester.</li></ul> Chemistry and Physics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47990 2026-07-27T16:14:06-05:00 2026-07-27T16:14:06-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - ESL <div>The Adjunct Instructor - ESL position in International Programs is responsible for teaching classes, maintaining related records, assigning and posting grades; maintaining appropriate office hours; and taking part in meetings and professional development activities as appropriate.</div> International Programs - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21552 2018-07-09T16:55:29-05:00 2023-03-23T10:50:33-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Quantitative Methods The Adjunct Instructor position in Quantitative Methods is responsible for teaching entry level statistics and operations management courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Quantitative Methods https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46794 2026-03-04T09:02:21-06:00 2026-03-04T09:02:22-06:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant <div>The Graduate Teaching Assistant position in Kinesiology and Health Promotion is responsible for teaching one-hour activity classes, assisting with research, and assisting faculty with classes.</div> School of Allied Health - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47686 2026-06-23T10:45:24-05:00 2026-06-23T10:45:25-05:00 Lecturer/Assistant Professor <div>The Lecturer/Assistant Professor position is a tenure-track faculty appointment in Art and Design with a primary focus on 3D media and interdisciplinary studio practice. The successful candidate will teach a range of three-dimensional processes that may include sculpture, ceramics, woodshop and fabrication techniques, digital fabrication, and emerging technologies relevant to contemporary 3D practice.</div><div>This position places a strong emphasis on integrating traditional analog methods with digital and technologically driven approaches, supporting students in developing conceptually rigorous and materially informed work. The faculty member will play a key role in developing, maintaining, and overseeing 3D studio facilities</div> Art & Design - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/44555 2025-06-24T10:30:59-05:00 2025-08-11T16:10:10-05:00 Adjunct - Legal Studies <div>The Department of Criminal Justice and Social Science is accepting applications for an Adjunct Instructor position in the subject of Legal Studies. This position is responsible for teaching Introduction to Legal Studies, Legal Research and Writing, Seminar in Legal Studies and Civil Liabilities.</div> Criminal Justice and Social Science - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47522 2026-06-03T09:58:35-05:00 2026-06-03T09:58:36-05:00 Helpdesk Technician <div>The Helpdesk Technician position in Information Technology is responsible for installing, troubleshooting, repairing and maintaining PC equipment; providing support for a wide variety of software applications and completing requests for new service in a dynamic, high-paced environment; and relying on instructions and pre-established guidelines to perform various other job duties.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48171 2026-08-11T16:05:58-05:00 2026-08-11T16:05:59-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in University Relations is responsible for taking photos at selected events, assisting in the collection and archiving of photos and photo releases, and assisting the Photography staff with additional duties as assigned.</div> University Relations - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21576 2018-07-09T16:56:42-05:00 2023-11-08T16:37:35-06:00 Adjunct Instructor - Applied Music The Adjunct Instructor position is responsible for teaching courses in Music. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Applied Music https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46980 2026-04-08T09:52:41-05:00 2026-04-08T09:52:42-05:00 Event Staff <div>The Event Staff position in Athletic Promotions is responsible for working at Basketball and Baseball games as ushers and ticket takers.</div> Athletic Director - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47873 2026-07-16T15:21:37-05:00 2026-07-16T15:21:38-05:00 Donor Stewardship Specialist <div>The Donor Stewardship Specialist will serve as a member of the Office of Development team and will play a key role in donor stewardship and fund management. The Donor Stewardship Specialist will work<strong> </strong>closely with the Development team and University colleagues to organize and review data to facilitate decision-making in support of engagement and stewardship strategies. This individual will identify and implement best practices to ensure that agreements and reporting are kept in University standards and meet donor expectations.</div><div>Duties and Responsibilities:</div><ul><li>Provide Annual Statements to donors</li><li>Deliver Monthly Fund Reports to appropriate colleges/departments</li><li>Work on gift agreements/scholarship agreements</li><li>Implement new donor recognition letters at all levels</li><li>Ensure all contributions are receipted in a timely manner</li><li>Produce and mail all monthly pledge reminders and recurring credit card donor reminders</li><li>Collaborate with Donor Relations on endowment reports, impact reports, donor/campus stories, etc. Gather all necessary data requested for those by connecting with Foundation Accounting, appropriate Colleges/Departments, Raiser’s Edge system, etc.</li><li>Quarterly review of all Foundation fund administration. Work with Development Officers and other Fund Administrators on fund purpose and utilization.</li><li>Assist in the process of awarding Foundation Scholarships each academic year. Work with all awarding parties and Academic Works manager in notification of awarding amount memos as well as what scholarship have not been awarded and need awarding throughout the academic year.</li></ul> Advancement Services https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48391 2026-09-03T09:01:24-05:00 2026-09-03T09:01:25-05:00 Web Master <div>The Web Master position in Information Technology is responsible for assisting with the development and publication of web content, working directly with faculty and staff to provide continuous maintenance and improvements to the university’s intranet portal and related websites.</div><div>This position reports directly to the Director of Web as part of a team that shares responsibilities and works collaboratively on a daily basis; assisting employees across the institution to build and enhance web-based tools to facilitate communication and deliver important information to all audiences; and assisting other divisions within the Office of Information Technology by working on projects that are not limited to the core responsibilities of the Web Division.</div> Information Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47701 2026-06-24T10:23:55-05:00 2026-06-24T10:23:56-05:00 Biology Specialist <div>The AMSTI/ASIM program at Troy University is seeking a qualified master teacher to work as a Biology Specialist with the Alabama Science in Motion Project. The position is responsible for the daily operations of the biology component of Science in Motion, including visits to high school biology classrooms in the Troy In-Service Region; and on-going documentation of equipment usage.</div> Science in Motion - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48314 2026-08-26T09:44:48-05:00 2026-08-26T09:44:48-05:00 Workship - Scenic & Properties Shop Assistant <div>The Workship position for the Department of Theatre and Dance is responsible for serving as a properties shop assistant, lighting technician and/or scene shop technician, including but not limited to assisting in implementing lighting design or scenic design, set up, operation, and breakdown for sets, props, and/or lighting; and organization and upkeep of current inventory.</div> Theatre & Dance - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/33860 2022-04-11T09:57:41-05:00 2022-04-11T09:57:42-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Interpreter Training <div>The Adjunct Instructor position in Division of CRIT is responsible for teaching courses in Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work.</div> Division of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47186 2026-05-06T08:52:13-05:00 2026-05-06T08:52:13-05:00 Graduate Teaching Assistant <div>The graduate teaching assistant will teach Physics, Physical Science, and Astronomy labs by effective delivery of the required course materials and fostering a positive learning environment for students.</div> Chemistry and Physics - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48010 2026-07-28T16:32:37-05:00 2026-07-28T16:32:38-05:00 Assistant/Associate Professor <div>The tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training position in the College of Education is an on-ground faculty appointment located at the Troy, Alabama campus. The position is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in clinical mental health counseling and other counseling specialties; maintaining an active program of scholarship, research, and professional contribution; advising and mentoring graduate students; supervising practicum and internship students; supporting CACREP accreditation and program assessment activities; and providing service to the department, college, university, profession, and community.</div> Department of C R I T - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21554 2018-07-09T16:55:34-05:00 2018-07-09T16:55:35-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Second Language Instruction The Adjunct Instructor position in Second Language Instruction is responsible for teaching related courses. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Leadership Development and Professional Studies https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46796 2026-03-04T09:04:50-06:00 2026-03-04T09:04:51-06:00 Workship <div>The Workship position for the Natatorium is responsible for assisting with the daily operations of the Student Recreation Gym and Natatorium.</div> Trojan Fitness Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/45464 2025-09-09T17:15:19-05:00 2025-09-09T17:15:20-05:00 Lecturer in Criminology <div>The Department of Anthropology, Sociology, and Criminology at Troy University seeks to hire a Lecturer to teach in our Criminal Justice and Legal Studies programs. The position is a 10-month appointment.</div> School of Social Sciences – Sociology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47524 2026-06-03T10:17:57-05:00 2026-06-03T10:17:58-05:00 Physics Specialist <div>The Physics Specialist position is responsible for recruiting high school science teachers to participate in AMSTI/ASIM; implementing a flexible communication system for scheduling labs; preparing activities/labs and supplies for the lab; submission of a weekly itinerary to ASIM Project Director; delivering activities/labs and supplies to participating AMSTI/ASIM teachers as scheduled; providing on-site support and mentoring for new or beginning teachers whenever possible; assisting with laboratory activities, delivering on-site professional development, and providing other training as needed; providing coaching to teachers to help increase their skills and move them to higher performance levels on the Alabama Continuum for Teacher Development based on the Alabama Quality Teaching Standards; coordinating work with the AMSTI site; picking up activities/labs and supplies from participating AMSTI/ASIM teachers in a timely manner; ordering, organizing, and maintaining activities/labs and supplies so they are readily available for classroom use; planning and implementing workshops to train high school science teachers to use AMSTI/ASIM activities/labs; teaching teachers the content background, how to use the activities/labs, and how to effectively lead students through the lab; planning and implementing workshops to train high school science teachers in other areas of science education such as laboratory safety, Science Course of Study, and other topics as needed; working with AMSTI/ASIM teachers and other specialists in developing new lab activities for high school students; attending statewide specialist meetings; participing in the continual improvement and implementation of AMSTI/ASIM; establishing and maintaining open communication with the SDE, project director and teachers; facilitating in a timely preparation and submission of the quarterly financial reports that include proper categorization of expenditures; organizing, properly updating, and promptly submitting Program Report information (visits, class roster, workshop attendance, AMSTI/ASIM inventory, and workshop agendas); communicating regularly regarding use of the AMSTI/ASIM activities/labs and training for AMSTI directors, project directors, system superintendents, principals, and teachers; facilitating the cleaning and maintenance of the AMSTI/ASIM vehicle; collaborating with AMSTI site director and specialist; and assisting AMSTI program with the development and piloting of the new activities/labs as requested.</div> AMSTI - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48188 2026-08-12T13:10:42-05:00 2026-08-12T13:10:42-05:00 Graduation Analyst I <div>The Graduation Analyst II position is responsible for, but not limited to: <br><strong>• </strong>Analyzing academic-programs in detail to ensure that all degree requirements have been satisfied for those undergraduate and graduate students. Determining that all paperwork has been properly submitted and approved for academic achievement.</div><div>• Ensuring academic requirements have been met for international student along with Coordinating with the International Office regarding 1-2-1 and 2-2 students’ academic requirements.</div><div>• Assisting in commencement ceremonies if needed.</div><div>• Answering questions related to graduation from phone calls or email messages.</div><div>• Assisting the Graduation Center with any other duties as assigned by the Director of the Graduation Center.</div> Graduation Center - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21581 2018-07-09T16:56:55-05:00 2025-10-13T11:16:30-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Counseling The Adjunct Instructor position in Division of CRIT responsible for teaching courses in Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training. Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester or term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Division of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46983 2026-04-08T09:54:56-05:00 2026-04-08T09:54:56-05:00 Security Officer <div>The Security Officer position in the University Police department is responsible for providing security patrols for the Dothan campus to ensure a safe and secure environment on campus.</div> University Police - Dothan https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47896 2026-07-21T14:55:06-05:00 2026-07-21T14:55:06-05:00 Workship <div>The Workship position in Assessment &amp; Technology is responsible for assisting the Technology Coordinator with the maintenance of computer labs and classroom technology in Hawkins Hall, including cleaning two computer labs and assisting with updating broken equipment for upgraded versions in 16 classrooms; and maintaining stock inventory of all needed equipment.</div> Assessment & Technology - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48393 2026-09-03T09:03:39-05:00 2026-09-03T09:03:39-05:00 Regional Recruiter - Houston <div>Troy University Regional Recruiters are an essential element of the University’s Enrollment Management team. This role will be tasked with supporting Troy Campus traditional freshman and transfer student recruitment efforts in a defined geographic region by implementing recruiting strategies and activities that grow the number of students applying to TROY, being admitted to TROY, and ultimately choosing TROY for enrollment. Duties will include constant contact to prospective students and their families as well as establishing positive relationships with high schools, community colleges, and other sources of potential enrollments. Regional recruiters reside in their assigned geographic areas, but will travel to Troy Campus several times a year for training and professional development activities. (All official travel is covered for reimbursement.)<br><br>PLEASE NOTE: Applicants must reside in, or be willing to relocate to, the assigned geographic territory.</div> Admissions - Troy Online https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47751 2026-07-01T10:04:32-05:00 2026-07-01T10:04:33-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant-Music Education <div>This position will work closely with the Coordinator of Music Education and Director of the School of Music. The responsibilities include:<br><br>1. Serve as a liaison between the School of Music and the Department of Teacher Education to coordinate clinical field placements for undergraduate Music Education students.</div><div>2. Support the maintenance of a database containing clinical field placement information.</div><div>3. Organize and update Music Education classroom inventory using a shared Excel spreadsheet.</div><div>4. Assist in maintaining a recruitment database for prospective Music Education students (choral graduate assistants will coordinate with choral faculty on a separate choral database, while band graduate assistants will work with band faculty to manage a database for prospective band students).</div><div>5. Contribute to the planning and coordination of Music Education Day.</div><div>6. Assist with all School of Music recruitment events.</div><div>7. Collaborate with music faculty and graduate assistants (Choral, Band, and Music Industry) to maintain a comprehensive School of Music recruitment database, including establishing consistent communication with prospective students and high school music teachers.</div><div>8. Support the management of the School of Music’s social media platforms.</div> Music - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48328 2026-08-26T14:30:24-05:00 2026-08-26T14:30:25-05:00 Director, Student Services Business Office <div>The Director position in the Student Services Business Office (under the supervision of the Controller's Office) assists the Student Services Department with management and oversight of fiscal operations to include tax compliance, budgeting services, payment services, monitoring of internal controls, and financial reporting to the Controller's Office.<br><br>Essential Functions:<br>- Advises, establishes, maintains, and monitors a strong system of financial and internal controls for the Student Services Department in coordination with the Dean of Student Services.<br>- Builds and maintains financial templates and reports as needed in the current financial reporting software. Prepares financial reports, department allocation reports, inventory reports or other specialized reports on a regular or ad hoc basis.<br>- Assists in the development of the annual budget as well as detailed monthly analysis of Student Services revenue and spend history. Reviews, analyzes, approves, and prepares budget transfers and other accounting allocations.<br>- Assists the Controller's Office and Foundation Accounting with the tracking, reporting, and compliance of all Student Services Department transactions. Prepares and reviews expense vouchers, invoices, purchase requisitions or other transactions for one or more departments, in compliance with approved budgets, University and/or Foundation policy and with appropriate delegation of tasks to the Student Services Staff Accountant.<br>- Assists with the fiscal year-end process and preparation of the annual financial report to include reconciliation and review of financial accounts or processes as needed throughout the year.<br>- Assist the Controller’s Office as needed and assume additional duties and responsibilities as assigned, including providing support for accounting, financial reporting, and other operational functions.</div> Controller's Office - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/36355 2022-11-17T16:07:32-06:00 2025-03-27T08:55:23-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - ASN Program <div><strong>ASN Program Adjunct Instructor</strong>&nbsp;<br><br>Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct Instructors hold the responsibility for the courses taught. Adjunct Instructors are expected to be available for a reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Adjunct Instructors may teach no more than 8 semester hours per semester.</div> ASN Program https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47257 2026-05-12T13:06:05-05:00 2026-05-12T13:06:05-05:00 Graduate Administrative Assistant <div>The Graduate Administrative Assistant position in the Division of Counseling, Rehabilitation and Interpreter Training is responsible for assisting the department chair and/or assigned faculty with any administrative duties related to research, assessment and accreditation information.</div> Department of C R I T - Troy https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/48012 2026-07-28T16:33:24-05:00 2026-07-28T16:33:25-05:00 Lecturer <div>The Lecturer in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training is responsible for teaching graduate-level counseling courses in a CACREP-accredited counselor education program. Responsibilities include course instruction, student advising and mentoring, clinical supervision of practicum and internship students, participation in curriculum development, support for student assessment and remediation processes, service to the department, and contribution to ongoing CACREP accreditation and program evaluation activities.</div> Department of C R I T - Global https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/21556 2018-07-09T16:55:40-05:00 2020-08-12T09:41:32-05:00 Adjunct Instructor - Biology Adjunct faculty members are employed to provide specific courses on an as-needed basis. Contracts for adjunct faculty members are issued on a semester/term basis. Adjunct instructors hold the responsibility for the management of courses taught. Adjunct instructors are expected to be available for reasonable amount of time for each course taught to counsel students regarding course work. Biology https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/46798 2026-03-04T09:07:21-06:00 2026-03-04T09:07:22-06:00 Workship - Writing Center Tutor <div>The Workship - Writing Center Tutor position in Instructional Support Services is responsible for tutoring Troy University students in writing improvement.</div> Learning Center - Troy"
