      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1076P Position Title Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor Position Type Faculty Department Department of C R I T - Global Division College of Education and Behavioral Sciences Campus Troy Online Faculty Rank If Faculty position 12 Month Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Dependent on selected rank Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location eTroy Job Summary The Lecturer/Assistant/Associate Professor position in the Department of Counseling, Rehabilitation, and Interpreter Training is a tenure-track faculty position for Clinical Mental Health Counseling. This position is primarily responsible for teaching specialized graduate courses in the clinical mental health program and core counseling courses within the specific area of expertise; pursuit of a scholarship and research agenda; service on committees at all levels; involvement in service to the community. This position also includes administrative responsibilities such as advising graduate students and supervising Practicum and Internship students, scheduling counseling courses, recruiting students for the program, proctoring and grading comprehensive examinations, attending faculty meetings, and attending required region meetings for faculty. In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. Earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP -accredited program by the date of appointment. 2. Professional identity as a counselor demonstrated through academic preparation, professional experience, and engagement in the counseling profession. 3. Eligibility for counselor licensure in Alabama (e.g., LPC or equivalent). 4. Academic preparation and/or professional experience in Clinical Mental Health Counseling, School Counseling, Rehabilitation Counseling, or a closely related counseling specialty. 5. Demonstrated ability to teach and mentor graduate counseling students in an online learning environment. Preferred Qualifications 1. Current professional counselor licensure ( LPC or equivalent). 2. Experience teaching in a CACREP -accredited counselor education program. 3. Experience supervising practicum and internship students consistent with CACREP standards. 4. Evidence of scholarship, research, grant activity, presentations, or publications in counseling or counselor education (required for tenure-track consideration). 5. Experience with online instruction, student retention initiatives, program assessment, and accreditation processes. Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? Driving may be necessary but is not a primary responsibility Work Hours Based on teaching schedules and departmental requirements. List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 07/22/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Academic Term Position Will Begin 2026 Fall Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47906 Reference Letters Reference Letters Last Day a Referen