    "https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47686": {
      "title": "Troy University Employment Site | Lecturer/Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Troy University Employment Site | Lecturer/Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Frequently Asked Questions Lecturer/Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number F1072P Position Title Lecturer/Assistant Professor Position Type Faculty Department Art & Design - Troy Division College of Arts and Humanities Campus Troy Faculty Rank Assistant Professor If Faculty position 10 Month Is this position tenure track or non-tenure track? Tenure Track Work Status Full-Time (FT) Temporary No Location Troy - T01 Job Summary The Lecturer/Assistant Professor position is a tenure-track faculty appointment in Art and Design with a primary focus on 3D media and interdisciplinary studio practice. The successful candidate will teach a range of three-dimensional processes that may include sculpture, ceramics, woodshop and fabrication techniques, digital fabrication, and emerging technologies relevant to contemporary 3D practice. This position places a strong emphasis on integrating traditional analog methods with digital and technologically driven approaches, supporting students in developing conceptually rigorous and materially informed work. The faculty member will play a key role in developing, maintaining, and overseeing 3D studio facilities In Class Teaching Percentage Online Teaching Percentage Minimum Qualifications 1. MFA in Studio Art with an emphasis on 3D media (such as sculpture, ceramics, or interdisciplinary studio practice) or a closely related terminal degree 2. Demonstrated expertise across multiple 3D processes, 3. Ability to teach and support both traditional analog methods and digital or emerging 3D technologies 4. Record of professional artistic activity appropriate to the rank of Assistant / Associate Professor 5. Strong commitment to undergraduate teaching and collaborative program development Preferred Qualifications 1. Experience in community/public arts interaction, entrepreneurship, and grant writing 2. Experience with the integration of traditional media with new technologies 3. Entrepreneurial experience Will this position require driving (personal vehicle, university vehicle, utility vehicle, or golf cart) in order to perform the job duties? No Work Hours To be determined List any hazardous conditions or physical demands required by this position N/A Does this position have supervisory responsibility? No Posting Date 06/23/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Qualified candidates must attach samples of scholarly writing and/or samples of creative work and/or samples of student creative work. Academic Term Position Will Begin Quick Link https://www.troyuniversityjobs.com/postings/47682 Reference Letters Reference Letters Last Day a Reference Provider Can Submit Reference Applicant Special Instructions Qualified applications will be made available to the department/committee for review immediately upon submission. We ask that you provide email addresses for your reference providers and please be certain that the email addresses you list are accurate. If you are selected as a candidate for consideration by the department/committee, an instructional email will be sent to your reference providers to ask that they submit a reference letter on your behalf via a link to our reference portal. Separate reference letters will be requested for each position to which you apply (if applicable), so your reference providers will be contacted separately for each application on which you list them. Reference letters will not be copied from one application to another. You can assure your reference providers that our system is secure and that all letters are confidential. If your reference providers have trouble using the reference portal, please advise them to contact jobs@troy.edu. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Troy University employment website (www.troyuniversityjobs.com) Chronicle of Higher Education Higher Ed Jobs Social Media website Indeed Other employment website (please specify below) Employee Referral (please specify below) Local newspaper (please specify below) Professional journal (please specify below) Other source (please specify below) Please specify: (Open Ended Question) * Regarding your current employment status, please select one of the following: Not a current Troy University employee Current part-time Troy employee (including adjunct faculty) Current full-time Troy employee - initial appraisal period complete Current full-time Troy employee - still within initial appraisal period (six months for new employees and three months for promoted employees) * Do you have a MFA in Studio Art with an emphasis on 3D media (such as sculpture, ceramics, or interdisciplinary studio practice) or a closely related degree? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Teaching Philosophy List of References Unofficial Transcript  1 Optional Documents Letter of Reference 1 Letter of Reference 2 Letter of Reference 3 Unofficial Transcript  2 Unofficial Transcript 3 Other Document - Employment is contingent upon a satisfactory background check. - Troy University is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action employer. - Troy University participates in eVerify. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
